{"_id":"213d97c2cbbd4f81","name":"Not in the Face","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"Prerequisites: Once per encounter, as a Standard Action, you may make a Persuasion check and use the result of the roll in place of your Reflex Defense until the beginning of your next turn. You can use your Persuasion modifier in place of your Deception modifier to Feint.","benefit":"Prerequisites: Once per encounter, as a Standard Action, you may make a Persuasion check and use the result of the roll in place of your Reflex Defense until the beginning of your next turn. You can use your Persuasion modifier in place of your Deception modifier to Feint.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"acb91d3803eb4fcd","tags":["action_economy","deception","defender","new_action","persuasion","skills","social","social_control","social_defense","standard_action","survivability","tree_acb91d3803eb4fcd","uncategorized_talent","feint","defense","reaction","fear","cowardice"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"hunter_pursuit_fear_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"implementedBy":"AbilityCombatActionResolver / GM-player context","notes":"Reviewed in T26 hunter/pursuit/fear cleanup. Conditional target, fear, pursuit, stealth, reaction, or minion effects should not mutate permanent actor totals.","phase26HunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Cowardice","status":"combat_action_card","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Reviewed in T26 hunter/pursuit/fear cleanup. Conditional target, fear, pursuit, stealth, reaction, or minion effects should not mutate permanent actor totals."},"combatActions":[{"id":"not-in-the-face","name":"Not in the Face","label":"Not in the Face","actionType":"standard","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Prerequisites: Once per encounter, as a Standard Action, you may make a Persuasion check and use the result of the roll in place of your Reflex Defense until the beginning of your next turn. You can use your Persuasion modifier in place of your Deception modifier to Feint.","notes":"Prerequisites: Once per encounter, as a Standard Action, you may make a Persuasion check and use the result of the roll in place of your Reflex Defense until the beginning of your next turn. You can use your Persuasion modifier in place of your Deception modifier to Feint.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"persuasion","when":"Use result in place of Reflex"},{"skill":"deception","when":"Feint substitution"}],"resources":["Once per encounter","Persuasion replaces Reflex until beginning of next turn","Persuasion can replace Deception to Feint"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"Self","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}]}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.405Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.reflex","turn.once-per-round"],"talentHunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Cowardice","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
{"_id":"247b9ba1f8d34683","name":"Retrovirus","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"Your mastery of genetic manipulation has extended to affecting those already alive and modifying how their genes are expressed. You can create a that allows a single Clone Scientist Trait to be expressed in a living being. Creation of the will only work for one individual and clones of that individual, and still requires all the costs and Skill Checks as if creating a clone of that person, with the addition of +20 increase to the Cloning DC. Further, each time a is used, the subject risks corrupting their DNA, and must resist an attack on their Fortitude Defense with an attack bonus of +5. A successful hit moves the target a Persistent -1 step on the Condition Track for cellular destabilization. At -5 steps, their DNA is hopelessly corrupted, and their cells break down, causing Death.","benefit":"Your mastery of genetic manipulation has extended to affecting those already alive and modifying how their genes are expressed. You can create a that allows a single Clone Scientist Trait to be expressed in a living being. Creation of the will only work for one individual and clones of that individual, and still requires all the costs and Skill Checks as if creating a clone of that person, with the addition of +20 increase to the Cloning DC. Further, each time a is used, the subject risks corrupting their DNA, and must resist an attack on their Fortitude Defense with an attack bonus of +5. A successful hit moves the target a Persistent -1 step on the Condition Track for cellular destabilization. At -5 steps, their DNA is hopelessly corrupted, and their cells break down, causing Death.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"8e44e56069274319","tags":["biotech","cloning","condition_removal","controller","crafting","defender","dual_wield","mobility","science","striker","sustained_damage","tree_8e44e56069274319","uncategorized_talent","medical","phase-t29-reviewed"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"retrovirus","name":"Retrovirus","label":"Retrovirus","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"Your mastery of genetic manipulation has extended to affecting those already alive and modifying how their genes are expressed. You can create a that allows a single Clone Scientist Trait to be expressed in a living being. Creation of the will only work for one individual and clones of that individual, and still requires all the costs and Skill Checks as if creating a clone of that person, with the addition of +20 increase to the Cloning DC. Further, each time a is used, the subject risks corrupting their DNA, and must resist an attack on their Fortitude Defense with an attack bonus of +5. A successful hit moves the target a Persistent -1 step on the Condition Track for cellular destabilization. At -5 steps, their DNA is hopelessly corrupted, and their cells break down, causing Death.","notes":"Cloning/retrovirus crafting reference. The Fortitude attack and persistent condition-track risk apply to the retrovirus subject when the created treatment is used, not to the talent owner passively.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Knowledge (Life Sciences)"},{"skill":"Treat Injury"}],"resources":["Clone Scientist trait expression","+20 Cloning DC","Fortitude attack +5 on use"],"requiredContext":["Single individual or clone line","Created retrovirus treatment"],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action_reference","applicationScope":"runtime_skill_crafting_medical_computer_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase29TechMedicalMicrotreeCleanup":{"phase":"T29","tree":"Cloner","status":"reviewed_manual_or_runtime_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Tech/medical/science microtree pass removed unsafe passive rows and surfaces crafting, cloning, poison, computer, droid-command, and treatment effects as truthful action/reference cards."}}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.406Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.fortitude","attack.when-hit"]}}}
{"_id":"2c27842384e55cb2","name":"Mercenary's Grit","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","benefit":"When you are affected by any debilitating condition, you can convert the condition's modifier from a penalty to a bonus for 1 round as a Swift Action. At the end of your next turn, move -1 step along the Condition Track.","description":{"value":"When you are affected by any debilitating condition, you can convert the condition's modifier from a penalty to a bonus for 1 round as a Swift Action. At the end of your next turn, move -1 step along the Condition Track."},"class":"f62ca2e639cab614","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","treeId":"4007fa87192b5884","tags":["action-economy","condition-removal","controller","force","force-control","mobility","soldier","sustained-damage"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.mercenarys_grit","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.407Z","detectedPredicates":["turn.on-current-turn"]}}}
{"_id":"2f6bdc483d8f4aa8","name":"Serene Courage","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"You may enter a brief meditative state as a Full-Round Action. You may remain in this trance as long as you wish, and you are still aware of your surroundings. However, you loses your Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense during your meditation. Upon emerging from the trance (a Swift Action), you may roll your first skill check or attack roll made in the following round twice, keeping the better result. You are immune to Mind-Affecting Fear effects.","benefit":"You may enter a brief meditative state as a Full-Round Action. You may remain in this trance as long as you wish, and you are still aware of your surroundings. However, you loses your Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense during your meditation. Upon emerging from the trance (a Swift Action), you may roll your first skill check or attack roll made in the following round twice, keeping the better result. You are immune to Mind-Affecting Fear effects.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"8955568285ba4115","tags":["action_economy","defender","force","mobility","new_option","ritual","spirit","striker","survivability","sustained_damage","swift_action","tree_8955568285ba4115","uncategorized_talent","phase-t28-reviewed"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual_or_runtime","applicationScope":"combat_action_or_force_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"serene-courage","name":"Serene Courage","label":"Serene Courage","actionType":"full-round","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"You may enter a brief meditative state as a Full-Round Action. You may remain in this trance as long as you wish, and you are still aware of your surroundings. However, you loses your Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense during your meditation. Upon emerging from the trance (a Swift Action), you may roll your first skill check or attack roll made in the following round twice, keeping the better result. You are immune to Mind-Affecting Fear effects.","notes":"You may enter a brief meditative state as a Full-Round Action. You may remain in this trance as long as you wish, and you are still aware of your surroundings. However, you loses your Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense during your meditation. Upon emerging from the trance (a Swift Action), you may roll your first skill check or attack roll made in the following round twice, keeping the better result. You are immune to Mind-Affecting Fear effects.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Attack Roll"}],"resources":[],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"notes":"T28 removed unsafe migrated modifier/effect data. This talent depends on Force-suite, target, equipment, ally, encounter, or table-position context and is surfaced as a truthful manual/runtime card rather than a passive actor mutation.","phase28ForceMicrotraditionCleanup":{"phase":"T28","tree":"Bomarr Monk","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Force/special-tradition microtree cleanup. Unsafe always-on rows were removed; final bonuses/effects require player/GM or future dedicated runtime owner."}}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.407Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.reflex"]}}}
{"_id":"395daa7cd6f14b8f","name":"Rough Landings","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Emergency Maneuvers, BAB +6","description":"- You automatically succeed on your piloting check to land while Sputtering or moving Full-Throttle. Also, if you’re conscious when landing with a deployed Emergency Chute, you take no damage from falling and aren’t knocked prone. Once per round, if something Grabs you and you have 6 squares of vertical space above you, then as an immediate reaction (including before any Grapple Checks), you can burn 3 charges to instantly escape the grab, ending your movement 6 squares up. Beings with Intelligence 2 or more can choose to try to maintain their grab: as a Swift Action, they can make a second Grab Check. If the weight of your equipment + your target + their equipment doesn’t exceed twice your Carrying Capacity, you drag them with you 6 squares up (they can use a free action to let go at any point in this ascent). However, if the weight exceeds twice your carrying capacity, you remain grabbed and stationary. If you're airborne and still grabbed, you can't automatically escape the grab on your turn. You must succeed on a contested grapple check. If you win, the grab ends and they either fall or activate their own fly speed as a reaction. If they win, the grab is maintained. Neither side may use grapple maneuvers (e.g., Trip, Pin). You can Activate your jet pack with a free action on your turn or at the start of a Surprise Round if you’re not surprised. If you have your Jumptrooper Qualification, you can also activate Full-Throttle Mode in the same turn that you Activate your jet pack. Refer to the talent of the same name from the Rocket Jumper Talent Tree, but the speed bonus applies only when in Hover and Sweep Mode. Refer to the talent of the same name from the Rocket Jumper Talent Tree. Like a carrion crow, you can grab your prey, gain altitude, and drop them to the ground. Once per encounter, if you still have your three actions available (Swift, Standard, Move) on your current turn and 12 squares of vertical space above you, then as a standard action, you can attempt a Grab per normal rules except that you don’t provoke an Attack of Opportunity and your attack penalty is only -2. If you succeed, as long as the weight of your equipment + your target + their equipment doesn’t exceed twice your Carrying Capacity, you immediately spend your move action to burn 4 charges and drag your target 12 squares straight up, then spend your swift action to release the target in a square next to you - these follow up actions can’t be delayed. You cause 2d6 bludgeoning damage from the rough handling. Instead of a grab, you can ranged grab with appropriate equipment (e.g., Snare Pistol, Whipcord, Shock Whip), but the target must be within 2 squares range. Your released target doesn’t fall to the ground until the beginning of your next turn, giving them and their allies a chance to prevent the worst outcome. (E.g., they could activate their own fly speed on their turn.) Otherwise, the GM determines the target’s Falling Damage for 18 meters at the beginning of your turn using normal rules. Full-Throttle Mode no longer applies a -2 attack penalty. When you’re in All-Out Movement Mode, as a free action once per turn, you may make one ranged attack with a pistol, rifle, or jet pack integrated missile launcher. This attack has a -2 penalty.","benefit":"- You automatically succeed on your piloting check to land while Sputtering or moving Full-Throttle. Also, if you’re conscious when landing with a deployed Emergency Chute, you take no damage from falling and aren’t knocked prone. Once per round, if something Grabs you and you have 6 squares of vertical space above you, then as an immediate reaction (including before any Grapple Checks), you can burn 3 charges to instantly escape the grab, ending your movement 6 squares up. Beings with Intelligence 2 or more can choose to try to maintain their grab: as a Swift Action, they can make a second Grab Check. If the weight of your equipment + your target + their equipment doesn’t exceed twice your Carrying Capacity, you drag them with you 6 squares up (they can use a free action to let go at any point in this ascent). However, if the weight exceeds twice your carrying capacity, you remain grabbed and stationary. If you're airborne and still grabbed, you can't automatically escape the grab on your turn. You must succeed on a contested grapple check. If you win, the grab ends and they either fall or activate their own fly speed as a reaction. If they win, the grab is maintained. Neither side may use grapple maneuvers (e.g., Trip, Pin). You can Activate your jet pack with a free action on your turn or at the start of a Surprise Round if you’re not surprised. If you have your Jumptrooper Qualification, you can also activate Full-Throttle Mode in the same turn that you Activate your jet pack. Refer to the talent of the same name from the Rocket Jumper Talent Tree, but the speed bonus applies only when in Hover and Sweep Mode. Refer to the talent of the same name from the Rocket Jumper Talent Tree. Like a carrion crow, you can grab your prey, gain altitude, and drop them to the ground. Once per encounter, if you still have your three actions available (Swift, Standard, Move) on your current turn and 12 squares of vertical space above you, then as a standard action, you can attempt a Grab per normal rules except that you don’t provoke an Attack of Opportunity and your attack penalty is only -2. If you succeed, as long as the weight of your equipment + your target + their equipment doesn’t exceed twice your Carrying Capacity, you immediately spend your move action to burn 4 charges and drag your target 12 squares straight up, then spend your swift action to release the target in a square next to you - these follow up actions can’t be delayed. You cause 2d6 bludgeoning damage from the rough handling. Instead of a grab, you can ranged grab with appropriate equipment (e.g., Snare Pistol, Whipcord, Shock Whip), but the target must be within 2 squares range. Your released target doesn’t fall to the ground until the beginning of your next turn, giving them and their allies a chance to prevent the worst outcome. (E.g., they could activate their own fly speed on their turn.) Otherwise, the GM determines the target’s Falling Damage for 18 meters at the beginning of your turn using normal rules. Full-Throttle Mode no longer applies a -2 attack penalty. When you’re in All-Out Movement Mode, as a free action once per turn, you may make one ranged attack with a pistol, rifle, or jet pack integrated missile launcher. This attack has a -2 penalty.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"25d99948c9cb41ad","tags":["action_economy","ambush","control","controller","feat_chain","heavy_weapons","mobility","move_action","new_action","offense_ranged","pilot","piloting","positioning","ranged","reaction","skills","standard_action","striker","support","survivability","sustained_damage","swift_action","talent_chain","trap","tree_25d99948c9cb41ad","uncategorized_talent","vehicle"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"jetpack_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"phase24TacticalRangedMilitaryCleanup":{"phase":"T24","tree":"Jumptrooper","status":"cleaned_runtime_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Unsafe passive/ActiveEffect data removed. Talent is represented by action cards, attack options, hit/critical riders, or explicit manual metadata as appropriate."},"combatActions":[{"id":"rough-landings-escape-grab","name":"Rough Landings: Escape Grab","label":"Rough Landings: Escape Grab","actionType":"reaction","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"When something Grabs you and you have 6 squares of vertical space above, burn 3 jet-pack charges to immediately escape upward before grapple checks as described by the talent.","notes":"When something Grabs you and you have 6 squares of vertical space above, burn 3 jet-pack charges to immediately escape upward before grapple checks as described by the talent.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Grapple","when":"Target tries to maintain grab"}],"resources":["Reaction","Burn 3 jet-pack charges","6 squares vertical clearance"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":""},{"id":"rough-landings-drop-attack","name":"Rough Landings: Drop Attack","label":"Rough Landings: Drop Attack","actionType":"full-round","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Once per encounter, if all three actions are available and 12 squares of vertical space exist, attempt the special Grab/drop sequence. This consumes your standard, move, and swift follow-up actions.","notes":"Once per encounter, if all three actions are available and 12 squares of vertical space exist, attempt the special Grab/drop sequence. This consumes your standard, move, and swift follow-up actions.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Attack Roll","when":"Special Grab"}],"resources":["Once per encounter","Consumes standard + move + swift","Burn 4 jet-pack charges"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":""},{"id":"rough-landings-all-out-shot","name":"Rough Landings: All-Out Shot","label":"Rough Landings: All-Out Shot","actionType":"free","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"While in All-Out Movement Mode, once per turn make one ranged attack with a pistol, rifle, or integrated jet-pack missile launcher at -2.","notes":"While in All-Out Movement Mode, once per turn make one ranged attack with a pistol, rifle, or integrated jet-pack missile launcher at -2.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Attack Roll"}],"resources":["Once per turn","Jet pack all-out movement","-2 attack penalty"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":""}],"manualResolution":true}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.408Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.with-ranged","turn.on-current-turn","turn.once-per-round","target.is-prone"]}}}
{"_id":"3df46d093b31411d","name":"Indomitable class feature","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"Rather than becoming completely detached from your mental state, you are able to filter through influences to selectively allow beneficial effects. Instead of being immune to all Mind-Affecting effects, you become aware of any Mind-Affecting effects which target you, and may choose to allow or deny each effect. You have this ability even while unconscious.","benefit":"Rather than becoming completely detached from your mental state, you are able to filter through influences to selectively allow beneficial effects. Instead of being immune to all Mind-Affecting effects, you become aware of any Mind-Affecting effects which target you, and may choose to allow or deny each effect. You have this ability even while unconscious.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"e35ee41362604227","tags":["balance","force","survivability","tree_e35ee41362604227","uncategorized_talent","will_defense","phase-t31-reviewed","force-adept","healing","use-the-force"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual_or_runtime","applicationScope":"manual_class_feature","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"modifiers":[],"notes":"Mind-affecting allow/deny behavior is class feature / GM adjudication, not actor static bonus.","combatActions":[{"id":"indomitable-class-feature-t31-reference","name":"Indomitable class feature","label":"Indomitable class feature","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"Rather than becoming completely detached from your mental state, you are able to filter through influences to selectively allow beneficial effects. Instead of being immune to all Mind-Affecting effects, you become aware of any Mind-Affecting effects which target you, and may choose to allow or deny each effect. You have this ability even while unconscious.","notes":"Rather than becoming completely detached from your mental state, you are able to filter through influences to selectively allow beneficial effects. Instead of being immune to all Mind-Affecting effects, you become aware of any Mind-Affecting effects which target you, and may choose to allow or deny each effect. You have this ability even while unconscious.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Target context"],"requiredContext":["Valid target confirmed"],"targetHint":"GM/player adjudicated target or context","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[{"type":"RUNTIME_CONTEXT_REFERENCE","id":"indomitable-class-feature-t31-context","label":"Indomitable class feature","summary":"Rather than becoming completely detached from your mental state, you are able to filter through influences to selectively allow beneficial effects. Instead of being immune to all Mind-Affecting effects, you become aware of any Mind-Affecting effects which target you, and may choose to allow or deny "}],"phase31FinalRemainingCleanup":{"phase":"T31","tree":"Force Adept","status":"reviewed_manual_runtime_or_existing_engine_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":0,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Final remaining tree pass. No unsafe legacy rows remained; talent is surfaced through action/reference cards, context rules, or existing dedicated engine ownership instead of passive fake bonuses."},"requiresRuntimeContext":true}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.408Z","detectedPredicates":[],"forcePrestigeCleanup":{"phase":"T9","status":"manual_or_runtime","scope":"manual_class_feature"}}}}
{"_id":"4632b4bf79044752","name":"Nature Sense","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":{"value":"Prerequisites: Trained in Perception, You ignore Concealment (including Total Concealment) from darkness. However, you cannot perceive colors in total darkness. Additionally, at close range (within 10 squares), you ignore Concealment and Cover for purposes of Perception checks, and take no penalty from poor visibility while Tracking. Homebrew Reference Book: Saga Edition All-Purpose Sourcebook As a Swift Action, you may use The Force to calm Hostile and Unfriendly Beasts. Make a Persuasion check; if the result equals or exceeds the targets' Will Defense, its Attitude immediately shifts to Indifferent. You can affect a number of creatures whose total combined levels do not exceed your Character Level. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Homebrew Reference Book: Saga Edition All-Purpose Sourcebook You gain the ability to comprehend any spoken language. This does not grant you the ability to speak an unfamiliar language, only to understand them through The Force. Homebrew Reference Book: Saga Edition All-Purpose Sourcebook"},"benefit":"Prerequisites: Trained in Perception, You ignore Concealment (including Total Concealment) from darkness. However, you cannot perceive colors in total darkness. Additionally, at close range (within 10 squares), you ignore Concealment and Cover for purposes of Perception checks, and take no penalty from poor visibility while Tracking. Homebrew Reference Book: Saga Edition All-Purpose Sourcebook As a Swift Action, you may use The Force to calm Hostile and Unfriendly Beasts. Make a Persuasion check; if the result equals or exceeds the targets' Will Defense, its Attitude immediately shifts to Indifferent. You can affect a number of creatures whose total combined levels do not exceed your Character Level. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Homebrew Reference Book: Saga Edition All-Purpose Sourcebook You gain the ability to comprehend any spoken language. This does not grant you the ability to speak an unfamiliar language, only to understand them through The Force. Homebrew Reference Book: Saga Edition All-Purpose Sourcebook","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"ed899f9f41fc1391","tags":["action_economy","beast_companion","cover","dark_side","defender","defense","force","force_defense","force_execution","leader","mobility","nature","perception","persuasion","positioning","skills","social","stealth","support","survival","swift_action","tree_ed899f9f41fc1391","uncategorized_talent","use_the_force","exploration","beast"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"survival_exploration_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"implementedBy":"AbilityCombatActionResolver / GM-player context","notes":"Nature Sense contains perception/tracking and beast-calming context. Removed unsafe Will defense modifier.","phase25SurvivalExplorationCleanup":{"phase":"T25","tree":"Beastwarden","status":"combat_action_card","notes":"Nature Sense contains perception/tracking and beast-calming context. Removed unsafe Will defense modifier."},"combatActions":[{"id":"nature-sense-calm-beast","name":"Nature Sense: Calm Beast","label":"Nature Sense: Calm Beast","actionType":"swift","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Use the Force/Persuasion context to calm hostile or unfriendly beasts as described by the talent. Compare the check to the beast's Will Defense.","notes":"Use the Force/Persuasion context to calm hostile or unfriendly beasts as described by the talent. Compare the check to the beast's Will Defense.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"useTheForce","when":"Force-assisted beast calming"},{"skill":"persuasion","when":"Attitude shift check"}],"resources":["Mind-affecting","Hostile/Unfriendly beasts","Total affected levels limited by character level"],"requiredContext":["Beasts must be valid targets for the attitude shift"],"targetHint":"Hostile or Unfriendly beast(s)","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[{"type":"PERCEPTION_CONTEXT","id":"nature-sense-perception","suppresses":["darknessConcealmentForPerception","closeRangeCoverConcealmentForPerception","poorVisibilityTrackingPenalty"]}]}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.411Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.will"]}}}
{"_id":"4d7d5a38d0394e4c","name":"Force Bond","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Strong in the Force","description":"Alternatively, by spending a Destiny Point, a bonded individual may make an attack roll against their partner, ignoring the effects of line of sight and line of effect (including Cover and Concealment). If the bonded individual dies, or you spend a Destiny Point to sever the bond, the may be given to any other willing being possessing the Force Sensitivity feat. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook","benefit":"Alternatively, by spending a Destiny Point, a bonded individual may make an attack roll against their partner, ignoring the effects of line of sight and line of effect (including Cover and Concealment). If the bonded individual dies, or you spend a Destiny Point to sever the bond, the may be given to any other willing being possessing the Force Sensitivity feat. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"6ac3416fb6aada56","tags":["controller","cover","defense","dual_wield","feat_chain","force","force_offense","skill_substitution","talent_chain","telekinesis","telepathy","tree_6ac3416fb6aada56","uncategorized_talent"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"mechanicsMode":"manual_or_runtime","applicationScope":"force_user_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase22ForceCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Alter","status":"cleaned_manual_or_future_runtime","notes":"Removed unsafe migrated static modifiers/effects. Talent requires Force-user activation, target, Force Point, suite, item, or encounter context and must not mutate actor totals passively."}}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.412Z","detectedPredicates":[],"forceTalentCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Alter","status":"cleaned_manual_or_future_runtime"}}}}
{"_id":"588c176b47724734","name":"Feign Harmlessness","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"Prerequisites: When you successfully Feint an opponent, you may designate one ally within 12 squares. Your ally treats the target as Flat-Footed until the beginning of your next turn. Once per encounter, as a Reaction to an attack, you may make a Persuasion check and use that result in place of your Reflex Defense against that attack.","benefit":"Prerequisites: When you successfully Feint an opponent, you may designate one ally within 12 squares. Your ally treats the target as Flat-Footed until the beginning of your next turn. Once per encounter, as a Reaction to an attack, you may make a Persuasion check and use that result in place of your Reflex Defense against that attack.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"acb91d3803eb4fcd","tags":["action_economy","controller","deception","defender","persuasion","positioning","reaction","skills","social","social_control","social_defense","support","survivability","tree_acb91d3803eb4fcd","uncategorized_talent","feint","defense","fear","cowardice"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"hunter_pursuit_fear_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"implementedBy":"AbilityCombatActionResolver / GM-player context","notes":"Reviewed in T26 hunter/pursuit/fear cleanup. Conditional target, fear, pursuit, stealth, reaction, or minion effects should not mutate permanent actor totals.","phase26HunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Cowardice","status":"reaction_registered","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Reviewed in T26 hunter/pursuit/fear cleanup. Conditional target, fear, pursuit, stealth, reaction, or minion effects should not mutate permanent actor totals."},"combatActions":[{"id":"feign-harmlessness","name":"Feign Harmlessness","label":"Feign Harmlessness","actionType":"reaction","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Prerequisites: When you successfully Feint an opponent, you may designate one ally within 12 squares. Your ally treats the target as Flat-Footed until the beginning of your next turn. Once per encounter, as a Reaction to an attack, you may make a Persuasion check and use that result in place of your Reflex Defense against that attack.","notes":"Prerequisites: When you successfully Feint an opponent, you may designate one ally within 12 squares. Your ally treats the target as Flat-Footed until the beginning of your next turn. Once per encounter, as a Reaction to an attack, you may make a Persuasion check and use that result in place of your Reflex Defense against that attack.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"persuasion","when":"Use result in place of Reflex against attack"}],"resources":["Once per encounter reaction to attack","Successful feint lets ally treat target flat-footed"],"requiredContext":["Incoming attack"],"targetHint":"Self / one ally within 12","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{},"reactionKey":"feignHarmlessness","reactionTrigger":"ON_ATTACK_DECLARED"}]}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.413Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.reflex","proximity.ally-nearby","turn.once-per-round"],"talentHunterPursuitFearCleanup":{"phase":"T26","tree":"Cowardice","status":"reaction_registered"}}}}
{"_id":"5e4a7f98b1e74326","name":"Adept Spellcaster","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"You may spend a Force Point reroll a Use the Force check to activate a Force Power with the [Dark Side] descriptor, but the result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse. Prerequisites: , Illusionary Disguise Prerequisites: , Dark Lore You may reroll a Use the Force check made for the following uses; Search Your Feelings, Sense Force, and Sense Surroundings. Prerequisites: , Dark Lore When you spend a Force Point to reduce your Dark Side Score by 1, you may choose to instead reduce your Dark Side Score by 2.","benefit":"You may spend a Force Point reroll a Use the Force check to activate a Force Power with the [Dark Side] descriptor, but the result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse. Prerequisites: , Illusionary Disguise Prerequisites: , Dark Lore You may reroll a Use the Force check made for the following uses; Search Your Feelings, Sense Force, and Sense Surroundings. Prerequisites: , Dark Lore When you spend a Force Point to reduce your Dark Side Score by 1, you may choose to instead reduce your Dark Side Score by 2.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"cfd358ef61fb47bd","tags":["damage_reduction","dark_side","deception","force","force_capacity","force_execution","force_point_spend","force_power_synergy","illusion","investigation","knowledge","resource_spend","scout","spellcasting","sustained_damage","tree_cfd358ef61fb47bd","uncategorized_talent","use_the_force","phase-t28-reviewed"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual_or_runtime","applicationScope":"combat_action_or_force_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"adept-spellcaster","name":"Adept Spellcaster","label":"Adept Spellcaster","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolu