{"_id":"747458ee63cd4a2a","name":"Defensive Roll","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Weapon Focus (Simple Weapons)","description":"As a Reaction, when an attack exceeds your Damage Threshold and moves you down the Condition Track, you can choose to spend a Force Point to make a and not move down the Condition Track (but still take damage as normal). You can use your Use the Force check modifier instead of your Initiative modifier when making Initiative checks. You are considered Trained in the Initiative Skill. If you are entitled to an Initiative check reroll, you may reroll your Use the Force check instead (subject to the same circumstances and limitations). Prerequisite: After activating the Talent, you can move up to half your speed. You deal +2 points of damage with Unarmed Attacks.","benefit":"As a Reaction, when an attack exceeds your Damage Threshold and moves you down the Condition Track, you can choose to spend a Force Point to make a and not move down the Condition Track (but still take damage as normal). You can use your Use the Force check modifier instead of your Initiative modifier when making Initiative checks. You are considered Trained in the Initiative Skill. If you are entitled to an Initiative check reroll, you may reroll your Use the Force check instead (subject to the same circumstances and limitations). Prerequisite: After activating the Talent, you can move up to half your speed. You deal +2 points of damage with Unarmed Attacks.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"11f99465ba4847e2","tags":["action_economy","condition_removal","controller","defender","defense","feat_chain","force","force_control","force_execution","force_offense","force_point_spend","martial_arts","mobility","offense_melee","reaction","resource_spend","scout","skills","striker","survivability","talent_chain","tree_11f99465ba4847e2","unarmed","uncategorized_talent","use_the_force","phase-t27-reviewed"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"defensive-roll","name":"Defensive Roll","label":"Defensive Roll","actionType":"reaction","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reaction","useLabel":"React / Note","description":"When an attack exceeds your Damage Threshold and would move you down the Condition Track, spend a Force Point as a Reaction to avoid the condition movement.","notes":"When an attack exceeds your Damage Threshold and would move you down the Condition Track, spend a Force Point as a Reaction to avoid the condition movement.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Force Point context","Use the Force check"],"requiredContext":["Reaction timing must be valid"],"targetHint":"","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{"reactionKey":"defensiveRoll","trigger":"ON_DAMAGE_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED"}}],"rules":[],"mechanicsMode":"contextual","applicationScope":"force_lightsaber_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"manualResolution":true,"phase27JediLightsaberMysticCleanup":{"phase":"T27","tree":"Force Warrior","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"notes":"Jedi/lightsaber/Mystic leftover pass removed embedded effects and surfaces activation/timing/target context through action cards or resolver rules."},"reactionKey":"defensiveRoll","grantedReactions":["defensiveRoll"]}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.416Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"77ab82670aa14f33","name":"Smashball Pass","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"You've mastered the art of making it easy for a catchback to receive your passes, regardless of their skill or distance. If you've Aimed with a Thrown weapon or object, you reduce the Range by one category for the purposes of that attack roll (for example, from Medium to Short Range). Additionally, if an ally has Readied an Action to receive a Thrown weapon or object from you, you can throw it to them as a Move Action, provided you Aim and the weapon or object is at least one size category smaller than you. This throw is automatically successful. At GM discretion, some objects may not be aerodynamic enough to work with this ability. As a linebreaker, you're expected to charge forth and break down the defenses of the opponents to create openings for your fellow players to score. When using the Charge Action, you can move up to double your Speed.","benefit":"You've mastered the art of making it easy for a catchback to receive your passes, regardless of their skill or distance. If you've Aimed with a Thrown weapon or object, you reduce the Range by one category for the purposes of that attack roll (for example, from Medium to Short Range). Additionally, if an ally has Readied an Action to receive a Thrown weapon or object from you, you can throw it to them as a Move Action, provided you Aim and the weapon or object is at least one size category smaller than you. This throw is automatically successful. At GM discretion, some objects may not be aerodynamic enough to work with this ability. As a linebreaker, you're expected to charge forth and break down the defenses of the opponents to create openings for your fellow players to score. When using the Charge Action, you can move up to double your Speed.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"bfc1356c66c74783","tags":["action_economy","charge","controller","damage_reduction","defender","mobility","move_action","positioning","ranged","smashball","striker","support","teamwork","tree_bfc1356c66c74783","uncategorized_talent"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"smashball-pass-t30-reference","name":"Smashball Pass","label":"Smashball Pass","actionType":"move","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"You've mastered the art of making it easy for a catchback to receive your passes, regardless of their skill or distance. If you've Aimed with a Thrown weapon or object, you reduce the Range by one category for the purposes of that attack roll (for example, from Medium to Short Range). Additionally, if an ally has Readied an Action to receive a Thrown weapon or object from you, you can throw it to them as a Move Action, provided you Aim and the weapon or object is at least one size category smaller than you. This throw is automatically successful. At GM discretion, some objects may not be aerodynamic enough to work with this ability. As a linebreaker, you're expected to charge forth and break down the defenses of the opponents to create openings for your fellow players to score. When using the Charge Action, you can move up to double your Speed.","notes":"You've mastered the art of making it easy for a catchback to receive your passes, regardless of their skill or distance. If you've Aimed with a Thrown weapon or object, you reduce the Range by one category for the purposes of that attack roll (for example, from Medium to Short Range). Additionally, if an ally has Readied an Action to receive a Thrown weapon or object from you, you can throw it to them as a Move Action, provided you Aim and the weapon or object is at least one size category smaller than you. This throw is automatically successful. At GM discretion, some objects may not be aerodynamic enough to work with this ability. As a linebreaker, you're expected to charge forth and break down the defenses of the opponents to create openings for your fellow players to score. When using the Charge Action, you can move up to double your Speed.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Ally context","Charge context"],"requiredContext":["Arena/charge/thrown-weapon context confirmed"],"targetHint":"GM/player adjudicated target or context","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[{"type":"SPORTS_COMBAT_CONTEXT_REFERENCE","id":"smashball-pass","label":"Smashball Pass","summary":"Smashball Pass is an arena/charge/thrown-object context talent. Apply only when the triggering smashball/Bantha Rush/charge context is confirmed."}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action_reference","applicationScope":"martial_protector_arena_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase30MartialProtectorArenaCleanup":{"phase":"T30","tree":"Smashball Pro","status":"reviewed_manual_or_runtime_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"T30 removed unsafe passive rows from martial/protector/arena/species leftovers and surfaced action, reaction, recovery, cover, and attack-rider context as truthful cards/rules."}}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.416Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"78955cbbe9504d7f","name":"Patient Builder","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"Prerequisites: Skill Focus (Mechanics), Cybernetic Surgery, You may upgrade a Cybernetic Prosthesis just as you would any other item via the Tech Specialist Feat, using any of the following benefits: Enhanced Dexterity: The limb provides a +1 Equipment bonus on all Dexterity-based skill checks. Enhanced Strength: The limb provides a +1 Equipment bonus on all Strength-based skill checks. Enhanced Capability: The limb provides a +1 Equipment bonus on all Mechanics and Use Computer checks.","benefit":"Prerequisites: Skill Focus (Mechanics), Cybernetic Surgery, You may upgrade a Cybernetic Prosthesis just as you would any other item via the Tech Specialist Feat, using any of the following benefits: Enhanced Dexterity: The limb provides a +1 Equipment bonus on all Dexterity-based skill checks. Enhanced Strength: The limb provides a +1 Equipment bonus on all Strength-based skill checks. Enhanced Capability: The limb provides a +1 Equipment bonus on all Mechanics and Use Computer checks.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"38d7c18ce4664c66","tags":["crafting","engineering","mechanics","skills","slicing","striker","tech","tree_38d7c18ce4664c66","uncategorized_talent","phase-t29-reviewed"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"patient-builder","name":"Patient Builder","label":"Patient Builder","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"Prerequisites: Skill Focus (Mechanics), Cybernetic Surgery, You may upgrade a Cybernetic Prosthesis just as you would any other item via the Tech Specialist Feat, using any of the following benefits: Enhanced Dexterity: The limb provides a +1 Equipment bonus on all Dexterity-based skill checks. Enhanced Strength: The limb provides a +1 Equipment bonus on all Strength-based skill checks. Enhanced Capability: The limb provides a +1 Equipment bonus on all Mechanics and Use Computer checks.","notes":"Cybernetic prosthesis upgrade/crafting reference. Use the Tech Specialist/customization workflow; do not apply these equipment bonuses to the owning actor until the upgraded prosthesis exists.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Mechanics"}],"resources":["Cybernetic prosthesis","Tech Specialist upgrade"],"requiredContext":["Skill Focus (Mechanics)","Cybernetic Surgery","Cybernetic prosthesis being upgraded"],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action_reference","applicationScope":"runtime_skill_crafting_medical_computer_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase29TechMedicalMicrotreeCleanup":{"phase":"T29","tree":"Mechanic","status":"reviewed_manual_or_runtime_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Tech/medical/science microtree pass removed unsafe passive rows and surfaces crafting, cloning, poison, computer, droid-command, and treatment effects as truthful action/reference cards."}}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.417Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
