es a -5 penalty on all Use the Force checks until the end of their next turn. Additionally, when any character participating in the takes damage that exceeds their Will Defense; all other participants take damage equal to the original damage minus their own Will Defense. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Use the Force"}],"resources":[],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":""}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"force_user_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase22ForceCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Sense","status":"combat_action_card","notes":"Removed unsafe migrated static modifiers/effects. Talent requires Force-user activation, target, Force Point, suite, item, or encounter context and must not mutate actor totals passively."}},"talent_tree":"Jedi Guardian","talentTree":"Jedi Guardian","tree":"Jedi Guardian"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.419Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.will"],"forceTalentCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Sense","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
{"_id":"81cd2a2473e248a0","name":"In Balance","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"As a Full-Round Action, you may make a DC 20 Use the Force check. If successful, you may spend a Force Point to negate Dark Side Points gained by activating Force Powers with the [Dark Side] descriptor in your Force Power Suite; you may negate a number of Dark Side Points in this way equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum 1). After successfully activating this Talent, you may not attempt it again for 24 hours.","benefit":"As a Full-Round Action, you may make a DC 20 Use the Force check. If successful, you may spend a Force Point to negate Dark Side Points gained by activating Force Powers with the [Dark Side] descriptor in your Force Power Suite; you may negate a number of Dark Side Points in this way equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum 1). After successfully activating this Talent, you may not attempt it again for 24 hours.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"dcac793cc9fe42a7","tags":["action_economy","balance","dark_side","force","force_capacity","force_execution","force_point_spend","force_power_synergy","resource_spend","survivability","sustained_damage","tree_dcac793cc9fe42a7","uncategorized_talent","use_the_force","will_defense","phase-t28-reviewed"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual_or_runtime","applicationScope":"combat_action_or_force_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"in-balance","name":"In Balance","label":"In Balance","actionType":"full-round","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"As a Full-Round Action, you may make a DC 20 Use the Force check. If successful, you may spend a Force Point to negate Dark Side Points gained by activating Force Powers with the [Dark Side] descriptor in your Force Power Suite; you may negate a number of Dark Side Points in this way equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum 1). After successfully activating this Talent, you may not attempt it again for 24 hours.","notes":"As a Full-Round Action, you may make a DC 20 Use the Force check. If successful, you may spend a Force Point to negate Dark Side Points gained by activating Force Powers with the [Dark Side] descriptor in your Force Power Suite; you may negate a number of Dark Side Points in this way equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum 1). After successfully activating this Talent, you may not attempt it again for 24 hours.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Use the Force"}],"resources":["Force Point context","Force Power Suite context"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"notes":"T28 removed unsafe migrated modifier/effect data. This talent depends on Force-suite, target, equipment, ally, encounter, or table-position context and is surfaced as a truthful manual/runtime card rather than a passive actor mutation.","phase28ForceMicrotraditionCleanup":{"phase":"T28","tree":"Jedaii Ranger","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Force/special-tradition microtree cleanup. Unsafe always-on rows were removed; final bonuses/effects require player/GM or future dedicated runtime owner."}}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.419Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"85e9699cee664641","name":"Identify Creature","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Trained in Use Computer","description":"As a Standard Action, you can make a Knowledge (Life Sciences) check against a DC of 10 + the CL of a single non-Droid creature. If successful, you grant all allies that can hear and understand you a bonus to their attack rolls against that creature. This bonus is equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum +1), and lasts until the beginning of your next turn. Choose a single Knowledge Field (Bureaucracy, Galactic Lore, Life Sciences, Physical Sciences, Social Sciences, Tactics, or Technology). If you fail a Knowledge check with that Knowledge Field, you can spend a Full-Round Action as long as you have access to a computer network to reroll the check. You use your Use Computer skill in lieu of your Knowledge skill, and keep the better of the two results. You may select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select this Talent, it applies to a different Knowledge Field. You use your experience in xenobiology to recall a creature's traits and abilities. As a Swift Action, you can select a single non-Droid creature within line of sight and make a Knowledge (Life Sciences) check against a DC equal to 15 + the creature's CL. If the check is successful, you immediately learn any two (your choice) of the following pieces of information: Creature's Base Attack Bonus or attack bonus with a particular attack Any one of the creature's Defense Scores Any one of the creature's Skill modifier The presence of any one special quality or Feat (you choose the special quality or Feat, and the Gamemaster reveals whether or not it is present) You can make a Treat Injury check in place of a Mechanics check to Build Object to create a variety of Poisons, using your knowledge of specialized chemicals. When using this Talent, the Hit Point modifier for crafting is equal to the Poison's Challenge Level (for example, Knockout Drugs (CL 2) have a Hit Point modifier of x2). One dose of Poison is equal in size to a Fine object. The complexity of a Poison is determined by its Challenge Level (CL):","benefit":"As a Standard Action, you can make a Knowledge (Life Sciences) check against a DC of 10 + the CL of a single non-Droid creature. If successful, you grant all allies that can hear and understand you a bonus to their attack rolls against that creature. This bonus is equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum +1), and lasts until the beginning of your next turn. Choose a single Knowledge Field (Bureaucracy, Galactic Lore, Life Sciences, Physical Sciences, Social Sciences, Tactics, or Technology). If you fail a Knowledge check with that Knowledge Field, you can spend a Full-Round Action as long as you have access to a computer network to reroll the check. You use your Use Computer skill in lieu of your Knowledge skill, and keep the better of the two results. You may select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select this Talent, it applies to a different Knowledge Field. You use your experience in xenobiology to recall a creature's traits and abilities. As a Swift Action, you can select a single non-Droid creature within line of sight and make a Knowledge (Life Sciences) check against a DC equal to 15 + the creature's CL. If the check is successful, you immediately learn any two (your choice) of the following pieces of information: Creature's Base Attack Bonus or attack bonus with a particular attack Any one of the creature's Defense Scores Any one of the creature's Skill modifier The presence of any one special quality or Feat (you choose the special quality or Feat, and the Gamemaster reveals whether or not it is present) You can make a Treat Injury check in place of a Mechanics check to Build Object to create a variety of Poisons, using your knowledge of specialized chemicals. When using this Talent, the Hit Point modifier for crafting is equal to the Poison's Challenge Level (for example, Knockout Drugs (CL 2) have a Hit Point modifier of x2). One dose of Poison is equal in size to a Fine object. The complexity of a Poison is determined by its Challenge Level (CL):","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"00cb74839a524276","tags":["action_economy","control","defender","droid","feat_chain","healing","investigation","knowledge","knowledge_creatures","leader","mechanics","mobility","new_action","poison","scaling","skills","slicing","social","standard_action","striker","support","survival","sustained_damage","swift_action","talent_chain","trap","tree_00cb74839a524276","uncategorized_talent","science","medical","phase-t29-reviewed"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"identify-creature","name":"Identify Creature","label":"Identify Creature","actionType":"standard","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"As a Standard Action, you can make a Knowledge (Life Sciences) check against a DC of 10 + the CL of a single non-Droid creature. If successful, you grant all allies that can hear and understand you a bonus to their attack rolls against that creature. This bonus is equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum +1), and lasts until the beginning of your next turn. Choose a single Knowledge Field (Bureaucracy, Galactic Lore, Life Sciences, Physical Sciences, Social Sciences, Tactics, or Technology). If you fail a Knowledge check with that Knowledge Field, you can spend a Full-Round Action as long as you have access to a computer network to reroll the check. You use your Use Computer skill in lieu of your Knowledge skill, and keep the better of the two results. You may select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select this Talent, it applies to a different Knowledge Field. You use your experience in xenobiology to recall a creature's traits and abilities. As a Swift Action, you can select a single non-Droid creature within line of sight and make a Knowledge (Life Sciences) check against a DC equal to 15 + the creature's CL. If the check is successful, you immediately learn any two (your choice) of the following pieces of information: Creature's Base Attack Bonus or attack bonus with a particular attack Any one of the creature's Defense Scores Any one of the creature's Skill modifier The presence of any one special quality or Feat (you choose the special quality or Feat, and the Gamemaster reveals whether or not it is present) You can make a Treat Injury check in place of a Mechanics check to Build Object to create a variety of Poisons, using your knowledge of specialized chemicals. When using this Talent, the Hit Point modifier for crafting is equal to the Poison's Challenge Level (for example, Knockout Drugs (CL 2) have a Hit Point modifier of x2). One dose of Poison is equal in size to a Fine object. The complexity of a Poison is determined by its Challenge Level (CL):","notes":"Make the listed Knowledge (Life Sciences) check against the target creature. On success, grant the listed ally attack bonus until the beginning of your next turn. The current source text also contains merged science-tree text, so resolve only the part that applies at the table.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Knowledge (Life Sciences)"}],"resources":["Non-Droid creature","Allies who can hear and understand you","Intelligence modifier bonus, minimum +1"],"requiredContext":["Single non-Droid creature","Knowledge (Life Sciences) check"],"targetHint":"","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action_reference","applicationScope":"runtime_skill_crafting_medical_computer_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase29TechMedicalMicrotreeCleanup":{"phase":"T29","tree":"Science","status":"reviewed_manual_or_runtime_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Tech/medical/science microtree pass removed unsafe passive rows and surfaces crafting, cloning, poison, computer, droid-command, and treatment effects as truthful action/reference cards."}}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.420Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.when-hit"]}}}
{"_id":"9319584186ce4228","name":"Dathomiri Hunter","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Move Object","description":"When you take the Aim Action with an Energy Bow, you need only spend a single Swift Action (instead of the normal two Swift Actions) as long as you have used the Sense Surroundings aspect of the Use the Force skill since the beginning of your turn. Homebrew Reference Book: Dathomir Field Guide Once per turn as a Free Action, you can expend one use of the Move Object power from your Force Power Suite to reroll an attack roll made with an Energy Bow. The result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse. Homebrew Reference Book: Dathomir Field Guide Prerequisites: , Intuitive Aim As a Standard Action, you may make a single attack with an Energy Bow against a target you sensed through the Sense Surroundings aspect of the Use the Force skill since the beginning of your turn. That attack ignores all Concealment and Cover from any source that is not resistant to Lightsaber attacks. Attacks made in this way that pass through Cover to reach the target deal one less die of damage.","benefit":"When you take the Aim Action with an Energy Bow, you need only spend a single Swift Action (instead of the normal two Swift Actions) as long as you have used the Sense Surroundings aspect of the Use the Force skill since the beginning of your turn. Homebrew Reference Book: Dathomir Field Guide Once per turn as a Free Action, you can expend one use of the Move Object power from your Force Power Suite to reroll an attack roll made with an Energy Bow. The result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse. Homebrew Reference Book: Dathomir Field Guide Prerequisites: , Intuitive Aim As a Standard Action, you may make a single attack with an Energy Bow against a target you sensed through the Sense Surroundings aspect of the Use the Force skill since the beginning of your turn. That attack ignores all Concealment and Cover from any source that is not resistant to Lightsaber attacks. Attacks made in this way that pass through Cover to reach the target deal one less die of damage.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"ad16f3e5f4f7441b","tags":["action_economy","controller","cover","defense","exotic_weapon","feat_chain","force","force_capacity","force_control","force_execution","force_offense","force_power_synergy","lightsaber","melee","mobility","new_action","offense_melee","ranged_control","scout","spellcasting","standard_action","striker","sustained_damage","swift_action","talent_chain","tree_ad16f3e5f4f7441b","uncategorized_talent","use_the_force","witchcraft"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"dathomiri-hunter","name":"Dathomiri Hunter","label":"Dathomiri Hunter","actionType":"standard","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"When you take the Aim Action with an Energy Bow, you need only spend a single Swift Action (instead of the normal two Swift Actions) as long as you have used the Sense Surroundings aspect of the Use the Force skill since the beginning of your turn. Homebrew Reference Book: Dathomir Field Guide Once per turn as a Free Action, you can expend one use of the Move Object power from your Force Power Suite to reroll an attack roll made with an Energy Bow. The result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse. Homebrew Reference Book: Dathomir Field Guide Prerequisites: , Intuitive Aim As a Standard Action, you may make a single attack with an Energy Bow against a target you sensed through the Sense Surroundings aspect of the Use the Force skill since the beginning of your turn. That attack ignores all Concealment and Cover from any source that is not resistant to Lightsaber attacks. Attacks made in this way that pass through Cover to reach the target deal one less die of damage.","notes":"When you take the Aim Action with an Energy Bow, you need only spend a single Swift Action (instead of the normal two Swift Actions) as long as you have used the Sense Surroundings aspect of the Use the Force skill since the beginning of your turn. Homebrew Reference Book: Dathomir Field Guide Once per turn as a Free Action, you can expend one use of the Move Object power from your Force Power Suite to reroll an attack roll made with an Energy Bow. The result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse. Homebrew Reference Book: Dathomir Field Guide Prerequisites: , Intuitive Aim As a Standard Action, you may make a single attack with an Energy Bow against a target you sensed through the Sense Surroundings aspect of the Use the Force skill since the beginning of your turn. That attack ignores all Concealment and Cover from any source that is not resistant to Lightsaber attacks. Attacks made in this way that pass through Cover to reach the target deal one less die of damage.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Use the Force"}],"resources":[],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":""}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"force_user_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase22ForceCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Dathomiri Witch","status":"combat_action_card","notes":"Removed unsafe migrated static modifiers/effects. Talent requires Force-user activation, target, Force Point, suite, item, or encounter context and must not mutate actor totals passively."}}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.421Z","detectedPredicates":[],"forceTalentCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Dathomiri Witch","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
{"_id":"933240d6581843b9","name":"Lasting Ichor Item","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"Prerequisites: Intelligence 17, , Ichor Creation Items you create through the Ichor Creation Force Power gain one applicable benefit as though enhanced by the Superior Tech feat.","benefit":"Prerequisites: Intelligence 17, , Ichor Creation Items you create through the Ichor Creation Force Power gain one applicable benefit as though enhanced by the Superior Tech feat.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"01e443d93e47f9c4","tags":["alchemy","crafting","empowerment","force","force_capacity","force_power_synergy","tree_01e443d93e47f9c4","uncategorized_talent"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"mechanicsMode":"manual_or_runtime","applicationScope":"force_user_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase22ForceCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Force Item","status":"cleaned_manual_or_future_runtime","notes":"Removed unsafe migrated static modifiers/effects. Talent requires Force-user activation, target, Force Point, suite, item, or encounter context and must not mutate actor totals passively."}}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.421Z","detectedPredicates":[],"forceTalentCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Force Item","status":"cleaned_manual_or_future_runtime"}}}}
{"_id":"9780298d28d64954","name":"Centerbreaker Charge","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"Improved Bantha Rush You are a legendary linebreaker in the smashball arena, your skill on either side worthy of the Suktub Trophy. You can do each of the following abilities once per encounter: Make a Charge attack. The distance you push a target with Improved Bantha Rush is a number of squares equal to your Strength modifier. Make a Charge attack. You can make Acrobatics checks to Tumble through Threatened Areas or an enemy's Fighting Space when you Charge. This does not count as Difficult Terrain; however, the DC to Tumble increases by 2 for each additional Threatened Area or enemy's Fighting Space you Tumble through. Make a Charge attack. At the end of the Charge, if you succeed on a Grab or Grapple check, the defender may not attempt to escape the Grab or Grapple until after the end of your next turn.","benefit":"Improved Bantha Rush You are a legendary linebreaker in the smashball arena, your skill on either side worthy of the Suktub Trophy. You can do each of the following abilities once per encounter: Make a Charge attack. The distance you push a target with Improved Bantha Rush is a number of squares equal to your Strength modifier. Make a Charge attack. You can make Acrobatics checks to Tumble through Threatened Areas or an enemy's Fighting Space when you Charge. This does not count as Difficult Terrain; however, the DC to Tumble increases by 2 for each additional Threatened Area or enemy's Fighting Space you Tumble through. Make a Charge attack. At the end of the Charge, if you succeed on a Grab or Grapple check, the defender may not attempt to escape the Grab or Grapple until after the end of your next turn.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"bfc1356c66c74783","tags":["battlefield_control","charge","controller","mobility","positioning","scaling","smashball","striker","teamwork","tree_bfc1356c66c74783","uncategorized_talent"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"centerbreaker-charge-t30-reference","name":"Centerbreaker Charge","label":"Centerbreaker Charge","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"Improved Bantha Rush You are a legendary linebreaker in the smashball arena, your skill on either side worthy of the Suktub Trophy. You can do each of the following abilities once per encounter: Make a Charge attack. The distance you push a target with Improved Bantha Rush is a number of squares equal to your Strength modifier. Make a Charge attack. You can make Acrobatics checks to Tumble through Threatened Areas or an enemy's Fighting Space when you Charge. This does not count as Difficult Terrain; however, the DC to Tumble increases by 2 for each additional Threatened Area or enemy's Fighting Space you Tumble through. Make a Charge attack. At the end of the Charge, if you succeed on a Grab or Grapple check, the defender may not attempt to escape the Grab or Grapple until after the end of your next turn.","notes":"Improved Bantha Rush You are a legendary linebreaker in the smashball arena, your skill on either side worthy of the Suktub Trophy. You can do each of the following abilities once per encounter: Make a Charge attack. The distance you push a target with Improved Bantha Rush is a number of squares equal to your Strength modifier. Make a Charge attack. You can make Acrobatics checks to Tumble through Threatened Areas or an enemy's Fighting Space when you Charge. This does not count as Difficult Terrain; however, the DC to Tumble increases by 2 for each additional Threatened Area or enemy's Fighting Space you Tumble through. Make a Charge attack. At the end of the Charge, if you succeed on a Grab or Grapple check, the defender may not attempt to escape the Grab or Grapple until after the end of your next turn.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Once per encounter","Charge context","Bantha Rush context"],"requiredContext":["Encounter use available","Arena/charge/thrown-weapon context confirmed"],"targetHint":"GM/player adjudicated target or context","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[{"type":"SPORTS_COMBAT_CONTEXT_REFERENCE","id":"centerbreaker-charge","label":"Centerbreaker Charge","summary":"Centerbreaker Charge is an arena/charge/thrown-object context talent. Apply only when the triggering smashball/Bantha Rush/charge context is confirmed."}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action_reference","applicationScope":"martial_protector_arena_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase30MartialProtectorArenaCleanup":{"phase":"T30","tree":"Smashball Pro","status":"reviewed_manual_or_runtime_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"T30 removed unsafe passive rows from martial/protector/arena/species leftovers and surfaced action, reaction, recovery, cover, and attack-rider context as truthful cards/rules."}}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.422Z","detectedPredicates":["turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"a0c4b4b252ee4c96","name":"Cortosis Staff Block","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Nikto Survival (Kajain'sa'Nikto)","description":"As a Reaction, you may negate a melee attack by making a successful opposed attack roll. The DC of the attack roll is equal to the result of the attack roll you wish to negate, and you take a cumulative -5 penalty to your attack rolls to use this Talent for every time you have used since the beginning of your last turn. You must have a Cortosis Staff drawn to use this Talent, and you must be aware of the attack and not Flat-Footed. You may spend a Force Point to use this Talent to negate an attack against an adjacent character. Morgukai warriors have trained their minds to resist the effects of Jedi mind tricks, and as such, gain a +5 bonus to their Will Defense versus any Force Powers with the [Mind-Affecting] descriptor. Whenever you make multiple attacks with a Cortosis Staff as a Full Attack Action, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by 2. You can take this Talent multiple times; each time you take this Talent, you reduced the penalty on your attack rolls by an additional 2.","benefit":"As a Reaction, you may negate a melee attack by making a successful opposed attack roll. The DC of the attack roll is equal to the result of the attack roll you wish to negate, and you take a cumulative -5 penalty to your attack rolls to use this Talent for every time you have used since the beginning of your last turn. You must have a Cortosis Staff drawn to use this Talent, and you must be aware of the attack and not Flat-Footed. You may spend a Force Point to use this Talent to negate an attack against an adjacent character. Morgukai warriors have trained their minds to resist the effects of Jedi mind tricks, and as such, gain a +5 bonus to their Will Defense versus any Force Powers with the [Mind-Affecting] descriptor. Whenever you make multiple attacks with a Cortosis Staff as a Full Attack Action, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by 2. You can take this Talent multiple times; each time you take this Talent, you reduced the penalty on your attack rolls by an additional 2.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"0a61ab9ece844326","tags":["action_economy","anti_lightsaber","block","burst_damage","controller","cortosis","damage_reduction","defender","duelist","feat_chain","force","force_defense","force_offense","force_point_spend","light_side","melee","melee_defense","offense_melee","positioning","reaction","resource_spend","scaling","striker","talent_chain","tree_0a61ab9ece844326","uncategorized_talent","phase-t28-reviewed"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual_or_runtime","applicationScope":"reaction_or_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"cortosis-staff-block","name":"Cortosis Staff Block","label":"Cortosis Staff Block","actionType":"reaction","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"As a Reaction, you may negate a melee attack by making a successful opposed attack roll. The DC of the attack roll is equal to the result of the attack roll you wish to negate, and you take a cumulative -5 penalty to your attack rolls to use this Talent for every time you have used since the beginning of your last turn. You must have a Cortosis Staff drawn to use this Talent, and you must be aware of the attack and not Flat-Footed. You may spend a Force Point to use this Talent to negate an attack against an adjacent character. Morgukai warriors have trained their minds to resist the effects of Jedi mind tricks, and as such, gain a +5 bonus to their Will Defense versus any Force Powers with the [Mind-Affecting] descriptor. Whenever you make multiple attacks with a Cortosis Staff as a Full Attack Action, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by 2. You can take this Talent multiple times; each time you take this Talent, you reduced the penalty on your attack rolls by an additional 2.","notes":"As a Reaction, you may negate a melee attack by making a successful opposed attack roll. The DC of the attack roll is equal to the result of the attack roll you wish to negate, and you take a cumulative -5 penalty to your attack rolls to use this Talent for every time you have used since the beginning of your last turn. You must have a Cortosis Staff drawn to use this Talent, and you must be aware of the attack and not Flat-Footed. You may spend a Force Point to use this Talent to negate an attack against an adjacent character. Morgukai warriors have trained their minds to resist the effects of Jedi mind tricks, and as such, gain a +5 bonus to their Will Defense versus any Force Powers with the [Mind-Affecting] descriptor. Whenever you make multiple attacks with a Cortosis Staff as a Full Attack Action, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by 2. You can take this Talent multiple times; each time you take this Talent, you reduced the penalty on your attack rolls by an additional 2.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Attack Roll"}],"resources":["Force Point context","Force Power Suite context","Cortosis/equipment context"],"requiredContext":["Adjacency/position confirmed by GM/player","Cortosis staff equipped"],"targetHint":"","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{},"reactionTrigger":"GM_ADJUDICATED_REACTION_WINDOW"}],"rules":[],"notes":"T28 removed unsafe migrated modifier/effect data. This talent depends on Force-suite, target, equipment, ally, encounter, or table-position context and is surfaced as a truthful manual/runtime card rather than a passive actor mutation.","phase28ForceMicrotraditionCleanup":{"phase":"T28","tree":"Morgukai Warrior","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Force/special-tradition microtree cleanup. Unsafe always-on rows were removed; final bonuses/effects require player/GM or future dedicated runtime owner."}}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.423Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.will","attack.with-melee"]}}}
{"_id":"a1ef8440f49847f1","name":"Linebreaker Charge","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"Bantha Rush Having to protect the passback, the centerbreaker has to leverage their strength to an even greater degree than the linebreakers to keep the defenders at bay. When using the Charge Action, you can move with your opponent while using the Bantha Rush feat. If you have the Improved Bantha Rush feat, you can move with them as many squares as you push them back.","benefit":"Bantha Rush Having to protect the passback, the centerbreaker has to leverage their strength to an even greater degree than the linebreakers to keep the defenders at bay. When using the Charge Action, you can move with your opponent while using the Bantha Rush feat. If you have the Improved Bantha Rush feat, you can move with them as many squares as you push them back.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"bfc1356c66c74783","tags":["action_economy","charge","controller","mobility","positioning","scaling","smashball","teamwork","tree_bfc1356c66c74783","uncategorized_talent"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"linebreaker-charge-t30-reference","name":"Linebreaker Charge","label":"Linebreaker Charge","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"Bantha Rush Having to protect the passback, the centerbreaker has to leverage their strength to an even greater degree than the linebreakers to keep the defenders at bay. When using the Charge Action, you can move with your opponent while using the Bantha Rush feat. If you have the Improved Bantha Rush feat, you can move with them as many squares as you push them back.","notes":"Bantha Rush Having to protect the passback, the centerbreaker has to leverage their strength to an even greater degree than the linebreakers to keep the defenders at bay. When using the Charge Action, you can move with your opponent while using the Bantha Rush feat. If you have the Improved Bantha Rush feat, you can move with them as many squares as you push them back.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Charge context","Bantha Rush context"],"requiredContext":["Arena/charge/thrown-weapon context confirmed"],"targetHint":"GM/player adjudicated target or context","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[{"type":"SPORTS_COMBAT_CONTEXT_REFERENCE","id":"linebreaker-charge","label":"Linebreaker Charge","summary":"Linebreaker Charge is an arena/charge/thrown-object context talent. Apply only when the triggering smashball/Bantha Rush/charge context is confirmed."}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action_reference","applicationScope":"martial_protector_arena_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase30MartialProtectorArenaCleanup":{"phase":"T30","tree":"Smashball Pro","status":"reviewed_manual_or_runtime_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"T30 removed unsafe passive rows from martial/protector/arena/species leftovers and surfaced action, reaction, recovery, cover, and attack-rider context as truthful cards/rules."}}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.423Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"a36f9a2eb2424f86","name":"Amphistaff Block","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Prerequisites: Weapon Focus (Amphistaff), Base Attack Bonus +5","description":"As a Reaction, you may negate a melee attack by making a successful Initiative check. The DC of the Initiative check is equal to the result of the attack roll you wish to negate, and you take a cumulative -5 penalty on your Initiative check for every time you have used since the beginning of your last turn. You may use this to negate melee Area Attacks. If you succeed on the Initiative check, you take half damage if the attack hits, and no damage if the attack misses. You must have an Amphistaff drawn and in the Quarterstaff or Spear Forms to use this Talent. You must be aware of the attack and not be Flat-Footed. Prerequisites: , Weapon Focus (Amphistaff), Base Attack Bonus +10 Once per encounter, as a Reaction, you may make an Amphistaff attack against a being whose attack you negated using the Talent. You cannot change the Form of the Amphistaff prior to making this attack (meaning, the attack can only be made with the Quarterstaff or Spear Forms of the weapon). Only non-area melee attacks can be riposted in this manner; you cannot use this Talent when negating the damage from melee Area Attacks. You treat an Amphistaff in Spear Form as a Simple Weapon (Ranged), not a Thrown Weapon, for the purposes of determining Range. Additionally, you may recall the thrown Amphistaff as a Swift Action, but it does not return until the end of your next turn. You have learned how to extend the range of an Amphistaff's Spit Venom. The Spit Venom attack range is increased to 20 squares (instead of 10 square), but attacks made beyond 10 squares incur a -2 penalty on the attack roll.","benefit":"As a Reaction, you may negate a melee attack by making a successful Initiative check. The DC of the Initiative check is equal to the result of the attack roll you wish to negate, and you take a cumulative -5 penalty on your Initiative check for every time you have used since the beginning of your last turn. You may use this to negate melee Area Attacks. If you succeed on the Initiative check, you take half damage if the attack hits, and no damage if the attack misses. You must have an Amphistaff drawn and in the Quarterstaff or Spear Forms to use this Talent. You must be aware of the attack and not be Flat-Footed. Prerequisites: , Weapon Focus (Amphistaff), Base Attack Bonus +10 Once per encounter, as a Reaction, you may make an Amphistaff attack against a being whose attack you negated using the Talent. You cannot change the Form of the Amphistaff prior to making this attack (meaning, the attack can only be made with the Quarterstaff or Spear Forms of the weapon). Only non-area melee attacks can be riposted in this manner; you cannot use this Talent when negating the damage from melee Area Attacks. You treat an Amphistaff in Spear Form as a Simple Weapon (Ranged), not a Thrown Weapon, for the purposes of determining Range. Additionally, you may recall the thrown Amphistaff as a Swift Action, but it does not return until the end of your next turn. You have learned how to extend the range of an Amphistaff's Spit Venom. The Spit Venom attack range is increased to 20 squares (instead of 10 square), but attacks made beyond 10 squares incur a -2 penalty on the attack roll.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"d5b60c4f058c4085","tags":["action_economy","battlefield_control","block","controller","exotic_weapon","feat_chain","melee","melee_defense","mobility","offense_melee","positioning","ranged","reaction","scout","skills","striker","support","swift_action","talent_chain","tree_d5b60c4f058c4085","uncategorized_talent","phase-t28-reviewed"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual_or_runtime","applicationScope":"reaction_or_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"re