ult of the attack roll you wish to negate, and you take a cumulative -5 penalty on your Initiative check for every time you have used since the beginning of your last turn. You may use this to negate melee Area Attacks. If you succeed on the Initiative check, you take half damage if the attack hits, and no damage if the attack misses. You must have an Amphistaff drawn and in the Quarterstaff or Spear Forms to use this Talent. You must be aware of the attack and not be Flat-Footed. Prerequisites: , Weapon Focus (Amphistaff), Base Attack Bonus +10 Once per encounter, as a Reaction, you may make an Amphistaff attack against a being whose attack you negated using the Talent. You cannot change the Form of the Amphistaff prior to making this attack (meaning, the attack can only be made with the Quarterstaff or Spear Forms of the weapon). Only non-area melee attacks can be riposted in this manner; you cannot use this Talent when negating the damage from melee Area Attacks. You treat an Amphistaff in Spear Form as a Simple Weapon (Ranged), not a Thrown Weapon, for the purposes of determining Range. Additionally, you may recall the thrown Amphistaff as a Swift Action, but it does not return until the end of your next turn. You have learned how to extend the range of an Amphistaff's Spit Venom. The Spit Venom attack range is increased to 20 squares (instead of 10 square), but attacks made beyond 10 squares incur a -2 penalty on the attack roll.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Attack Roll"}],"resources":["Once per encounter"],"requiredContext":["Ally context confirmed","Amphistaff equipped"],"targetHint":"GM/player adjudicated target or affected creature(s)","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{},"reactionTrigger":"GM_ADJUDICATED_REACTION_WINDOW"}],"rules":[],"notes":"T28 removed unsafe migrated modifier/effect data. This talent depends on Force-suite, target, equipment, ally, encounter, or table-position context and is surfaced as a truthful manual/runtime card rather than a passive actor mutation.","phase28ForceMicrotraditionCleanup":{"phase":"T28","tree":"Master Of The Amphistaff","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Force/special-tradition microtree cleanup. Unsafe always-on rows were removed; final bonuses/effects require player/GM or future dedicated runtime owner."}}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.423Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.when-hit","attack.with-melee","attack.with-ranged","turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"a4629f24bd571414","name":"Mercenary's Determination","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Mercenary's Grit","benefit":"As a Free Action, on your turn, you can spend a Force Point to double your speed for 1 round. You must wait 5 rounds between each use of this ability.","description":{"value":"As a Free Action, on your turn, you can spend a Force Point to double your speed for 1 round. You must wait 5 rounds between each use of this ability."},"class":"f62ca2e639cab614","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.mercenarys_grit"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"4007fa87192b5884","tags":["feat-chain","mobility","soldier","sustained-damage","talent-chain"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.mercenarys_determination","migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.423Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"a9a84d42b75f4fb1","name":"Lesser Mark of Illumination","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"Those who have been illuminated can withstand immense physical pain and torture. You are granted a bonus to your Damage Threshold equal to your Wisdom modifier. Prerequisites: , Greater Mark of Illumination Achievers of Chalactan Enlightenment are masters of within. You may spend a Force Point to become immune to all Mind-Affecting effects for the remainder of the encounter.","benefit":"Those who have been illuminated can withstand immense physical pain and torture. You are granted a bonus to your Damage Threshold equal to your Wisdom modifier. Prerequisites: , Greater Mark of Illumination Achievers of Chalactan Enlightenment are masters of within. You may spend a Force Point to become immune to all Mind-Affecting effects for the remainder of the encounter.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"f3881205595248d4","tags":["defender","force","force_item","force_offense","force_point_spend","illumination","leader","light_side","resource_spend","striker","tree_f3881205595248d4","uncategorized_talent","phase-t28-reviewed"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual_or_runtime","applicationScope":"combat_action_or_force_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"lesser-mark-of-illumination","name":"Lesser Mark of Illumination","label":"Lesser Mark of Illumination","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"Those who have been illuminated can withstand immense physical pain and torture. You are granted a bonus to your Damage Threshold equal to your Wisdom modifier. Prerequisites: , Greater Mark of Illumination Achievers of Chalactan Enlightenment are masters of within. You may spend a Force Point to become immune to all Mind-Affecting effects for the remainder of the encounter.","notes":"Those who have been illuminated can withstand immense physical pain and torture. You are granted a bonus to your Damage Threshold equal to your Wisdom modifier. Prerequisites: , Greater Mark of Illumination Achievers of Chalactan Enlightenment are masters of within. You may spend a Force Point to become immune to all Mind-Affecting effects for the remainder of the encounter.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Force Point context"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"notes":"T28 removed unsafe migrated modifier/effect data. This talent depends on Force-suite, target, equipment, ally, encounter, or table-position context and is surfaced as a truthful manual/runtime card rather than a passive actor mutation.","phase28ForceMicrotraditionCleanup":{"phase":"T28","tree":"Chalactan Adept","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Force/special-tradition microtree cleanup. Unsafe always-on rows were removed; final bonuses/effects require player/GM or future dedicated runtime owner."}}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.424Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"b1669310f65d42b7","name":"Engineering Savant","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"Prerequisites: Skill Focus (Mechanics), Gearhead, , Patient Builder When you use the Tech Specialist feat on a weapon or suit of armor that you are proficient with, or a device, Droid, or Vehicle that you are familiar with (GM's call), you may pay twice as much for the parts to add the trait, but the trait does not count towards the one-per-item limit of traits. You cannot apply the same trait to the same item twice, and you may only use this Talent once per item that you upgrade.","benefit":"Prerequisites: Skill Focus (Mechanics), Gearhead, , Patient Builder When you use the Tech Specialist feat on a weapon or suit of armor that you are proficient with, or a device, Droid, or Vehicle that you are familiar with (GM's call), you may pay twice as much for the parts to add the trait, but the trait does not count towards the one-per-item limit of traits. You cannot apply the same trait to the same item twice, and you may only use this Talent once per item that you upgrade.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"38d7c18ce4664c66","tags":["armor","crafting","defender","droid","engineering","mechanics","pilot","skills","striker","tech","tree_38d7c18ce4664c66","uncategorized_talent","vehicle","phase-t29-reviewed"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"engineering-savant","name":"Engineering Savant","label":"Engineering Savant","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"Prerequisites: Skill Focus (Mechanics), Gearhead, , Patient Builder When you use the Tech Specialist feat on a weapon or suit of armor that you are proficient with, or a device, Droid, or Vehicle that you are familiar with (GM's call), you may pay twice as much for the parts to add the trait, but the trait does not count towards the one-per-item limit of traits. You cannot apply the same trait to the same item twice, and you may only use this Talent once per item that you upgrade.","notes":"Tech Specialist crafting reference. Pay the increased parts cost to add a trait without counting against the normal one-trait limit, subject to the once-per-item restriction.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Mechanics"}],"resources":["Tech Specialist upgrade","Double parts cost","Once per item"],"requiredContext":["Appropriate item/device/droid/vehicle familiarity","Trait is not already applied"],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action_reference","applicationScope":"runtime_skill_crafting_medical_computer_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase29TechMedicalMicrotreeCleanup":{"phase":"T29","tree":"Mechanic","status":"reviewed_manual_or_runtime_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Tech/medical/science microtree pass removed unsafe passive rows and surfaces crafting, cloning, poison, computer, droid-command, and treatment effects as truthful action/reference cards."}}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.425Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"b431ca7ea00947b9","name":"Delusion","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"You may create a predefined illusion designed to delude a single target. The delusion persists in the target's senses for 1d4 rounds. You then move down two steps on the Condition Track after creating the . You may use your Use the Force check modifier instead of your Deception check for purposes of Deceptive Appearance. You are considered Trained in the Deception skill for the purposes of using this Talent. If you are entitled to a Deception check reroll for Deceptive Appearance, you may reroll your Use the Force check instead.","benefit":"You may create a predefined illusion designed to delude a single target. The delusion persists in the target's senses for 1d4 rounds. You then move down two steps on the Condition Track after creating the . You may use your Use the Force check modifier instead of your Deception check for purposes of Deceptive Appearance. You are considered Trained in the Deception skill for the purposes of using this Talent. If you are entitled to a Deception check reroll for Deceptive Appearance, you may reroll your Use the Force check instead.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"cfd358ef61fb47bd","tags":["condition_removal","controller","deception","force","force_control","force_execution","illusion","mobility","perception","scout","skills","social","social_control","spellcasting","striker","sustained_damage","tree_cfd358ef61fb47bd","uncategorized_talent","use_the_force","phase-t28-reviewed"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual_or_runtime","applicationScope":"combat_action_or_force_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"delusion","name":"Delusion","label":"Delusion","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"You may create a predefined illusion designed to delude a single target. The delusion persists in the target's senses for 1d4 rounds. You then move down two steps on the Condition Track after creating the . You may use your Use the Force check modifier instead of your Deception check for purposes of Deceptive Appearance. You are considered Trained in the Deception skill for the purposes of using this Talent. If you are entitled to a Deception check reroll for Deceptive Appearance, you may reroll your Use the Force check instead.","notes":"You may create a predefined illusion designed to delude a single target. The delusion persists in the target's senses for 1d4 rounds. You then move down two steps on the Condition Track after creating the . You may use your Use the Force check modifier instead of your Deception check for purposes of Deceptive Appearance. You are considered Trained in the Deception skill for the purposes of using this Talent. If you are entitled to a Deception check reroll for Deceptive Appearance, you may reroll your Use the Force check instead.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Use the Force"},{"skill":"Perception"}],"resources":["Condition Track context"],"requiredContext":["Target context confirmed"],"targetHint":"GM/player adjudicated target or affected creature(s)","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"notes":"T28 removed unsafe migrated modifier/effect data. This talent depends on Force-suite, target, equipment, ally, encounter, or table-position context and is surfaced as a truthful manual/runtime card rather than a passive actor mutation.","phase28ForceMicrotraditionCleanup":{"phase":"T28","tree":"Sorcerer Of Tund","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Force/special-tradition microtree cleanup. Unsafe always-on rows were removed; final bonuses/effects require player/GM or future dedicated runtime owner."}}},"effects":