{"_id":"b9fce171cad543d7","name":"Clone Scientist","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"Trained in Knowledge (Life Sciences) You have unlocked the secrets of combining the genes of a variety of creatures to create mutations and even new Species. When you create a gene-spliced clone, first select a DNA template as normal. Next, you may add additional template Species, each time adding either one method of movement, one natural weapon, or one Species Trait or special quality. Every additional Species spliced adds +10 to the cloning attempt DC. Each new form of movement adds +10 to the DC, each new natural weapon/attack adds +5 to the DC, and each Species Trait or special quality adds +10 to the DC. Spliced Traits can stack with and Master Cloner traits. Prerequisites: , Trained in Knowledge (Life Sciences) Prerequisites: , Trained in Knowledge (Life Sciences) When cloning, you may select advanced traits for the clone, listed below. These traits may be selected in tandem with the Clone Scientist Traits, unless stated otherwise. Prerequisites: , Trained in Knowledge (Life Sciences) You have found ways to increase the rate of aging of clones to more quickly put them in service. The overall cost of the creation of the clone is increased by the age modifier. When a clone whose age has been accelerated moves at least -2 steps down the Condition Track in the same encounter, they also add a year to their relative Age. Also note that while accelerated Aging brings the clones to physical maturity more quickly, mentally, they progress at their actual physical age. This means that a Human clone who is engineered to age twice as fast as normal, will be a physical adult after eight years (Humans are Adults at 16-40 years old), giving them no modifiers of a Child to Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma until they are twelve years old (twenty-four in clone years). Prerequisites: , Master Cloner, Trained in Knowledge (Life Sciences)","benefit":"Trained in Knowledge (Life Sciences) You have unlocked the secrets of combining the genes of a variety of creatures to create mutations and even new Species. When you create a gene-spliced clone, first select a DNA template as normal. Next, you may add additional template Species, each time adding either one method of movement, one natural weapon, or one Species Trait or special quality. Every additional Species spliced adds +10 to the cloning attempt DC. Each new form of movement adds +10 to the DC, each new natural weapon/attack adds +5 to the DC, and each Species Trait or special quality adds +10 to the DC. Spliced Traits can stack with and Master Cloner traits. Prerequisites: , Trained in Knowledge (Life Sciences) Prerequisites: , Trained in Knowledge (Life Sciences) When cloning, you may select advanced traits for the clone, listed below. These traits may be selected in tandem with the Clone Scientist Traits, unless stated otherwise. Prerequisites: , Trained in Knowledge (Life Sciences) You have found ways to increase the rate of aging of clones to more quickly put them in service. The overall cost of the creation of the clone is increased by the age modifier. When a clone whose age has been accelerated moves at least -2 steps down the Condition Track in the same encounter, they also add a year to their relative Age. Also note that while accelerated Aging brings the clones to physical maturity more quickly, mentally, they progress at their actual physical age. This means that a Human clone who is engineered to age twice as fast as normal, will be a physical adult after eight years (Humans are Adults at 16-40 years old), giving them no modifiers of a Child to Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma until they are twelve years old (twenty-four in clone years). Prerequisites: , Master Cloner, Trained in Knowledge (Life Sciences)","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"8e44e56069274319","tags":["biotech","cloning","condition_removal","controller","crafting","investigation","knowledge","mobility","scaling","science","striker","support","tree_8e44e56069274319","uncategorized_talent","medical","phase-t29-reviewed"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"clone-scientist","name":"Clone Scientist","label":"Clone Scientist","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"Trained in Knowledge (Life Sciences) You have unlocked the secrets of combining the genes of a variety of creatures to create mutations and even new Species. When you create a gene-spliced clone, first select a DNA template as normal. Next, you may add additional template Species, each time adding either one method of movement, one natural weapon, or one Species Trait or special quality. Every additional Species spliced adds +10 to the cloning attempt DC. Each new form of movement adds +10 to the DC, each new natural weapon/attack adds +5 to the DC, and each Species Trait or special quality adds +10 to the DC. Spliced Traits can stack with and Master Cloner traits. Prerequisites: , Trained in Knowledge (Life Sciences) Prerequisites: , Trained in Knowledge (Life Sciences) When cloning, you may select advanced traits for the clone, listed below. These traits may be selected in tandem with the Clone Scientist Traits, unless stated otherwise. Prerequisites: , Trained in Knowledge (Life Sciences) You have found ways to increase the rate of aging of clones to more quickly put them in service. The overall cost of the creation of the clone is increased by the age modifier. When a clone whose age has been accelerated moves at least -2 steps down the Condition Track in the same encounter, they also add a year to their relative Age. Also note that while accelerated Aging brings the clones to physical maturity more quickly, mentally, they progress at their actual physical age. This means that a Human clone who is engineered to age twice as fast as normal, will be a physical adult after eight years (Humans are Adults at 16-40 years old), giving them no modifiers of a Child to Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma until they are twelve years old (twenty-four in clone years). Prerequisites: , Master Cloner, Trained in Knowledge (Life Sciences)","notes":"Clone design reference. The current compendium text is merged from multiple cloning entries, so this card intentionally avoids automatic mutations and leaves template/trait/cost/DC selection to the cloning workflow or GM.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Knowledge (Life Sciences)"}],"resources":["Gene-spliced clone","Additional species templates","Clone Scientist traits"],"requiredContext":["Trained in Knowledge (Life Sciences)","Cloning project"],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action_reference","applicationScope":"runtime_skill_crafting_medical_computer_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase29TechMedicalMicrotreeCleanup":{"phase":"T29","tree":"Cloner","status":"reviewed_manual_or_runtime_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Tech/medical/science microtree pass removed unsafe passive rows and surfaces crafting, cloning, poison, computer, droid-command, and treatment effects as truthful action/reference cards."}}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.426Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"cc1cf3a694244618","name":"Diplomatic Poise","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"The strength of your personality is incomparable. Once per encounter, as a Reaction, you may use your Will Defense as your Fortitude Defense. This will also affect Damage Threshold until your next turn.","benefit":"The strength of your personality is incomparable. Once per encounter, as a Reaction, you may use your Will Defense as your Fortitude Defense. This will also affect Damage Threshold until your next turn.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"feb08c2834a447ab","tags":["action_economy","defender","diplomacy","leader","reaction","social_defense","striker","tree_feb08c2834a447ab","uncategorized_talent"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","applicationScope":"social_commander_runtime_context","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"combatActions":[{"id":"diplomatic-poise","name":"Diplomatic Poise","label":"Diplomatic Poise","actionType":"reaction","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"Once per encounter, use your Will Defense as your Fortitude Defense, also affecting Damage Threshold, until your next turn.","notes":"Once per encounter, use your Will Defense as your Fortitude Defense, also affecting Damage Threshold, until your next turn.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Once per encounter"],"requiredContext":["Incoming effect checks Fortitude or Damage Threshold"],"targetHint":"Self","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","manualResolution":true,"phase23SocialCommanderCleanup":{"phase":"T23","tree":"Galactic Senator","status":"combat_action_card","cardsAdded":1,"notes":"Social/commander activation surfaced through abilityMeta combat action cards. Skill-backed cards use the existing sheet skill preroller where safe; final buffs/debuffs remain GM/player/runtime-applied."}}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.428Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.fortitude","defense.will","turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"cc78c981176d4fed","name":"Avoid Collisions","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"- You can always attempt to Avoid a Collision for half damage. If you were permitted to avoid a collision without this talent, you instead take half-damage on a failure and no damage on a success.","benefit":"- You can always attempt to Avoid a Collision for half damage. If you were permitted to avoid a collision without this talent, you instead take half-damage on a failure and no damage on a success.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"25d99948c9cb41ad","tags":["evasion","mobility","pilot","striker","survivability","tree_25d99948c9cb41ad","uncategorized_talent","vehicle"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"jetpack_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"phase24TacticalRangedMilitaryCleanup":{"phase":"T24","tree":"Jumptrooper","status":"cleaned_runtime_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Unsafe passive/ActiveEffect data removed. Talent is represented by action cards, attack options, hit/critical riders, or explicit manual metadata as appropriate."},"combatActions":[{"id":"avoid-collisions","name":"Avoid Collisions","label":"Avoid Collisions","actionType":"reaction","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"You can always attempt to avoid a collision for half damage. If normally allowed to avoid it, success means no damage and failure means half damage.","notes":"You can always attempt to avoid a collision for half damage. If normally allowed to avoid it, success means no damage and failure means half damage.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Collision context"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":""}],"manualResolution":true}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.428Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"d1418afeaa3f40ec","name":"Reflexive Tilting","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"- Your effortless adjustments in flight just by shifting weight make you a little more elusive than when you're on the ground. While airborne and with your jet pack Active, you gain a dodge bonus of +1 to your Reflex Defense. This bonus stacks with other applicable dodge bonuses, and you lose all dodge bonuses when you would lose a Dexterity bonus to your Reflex Defense.","benefit":"- Your effortless adjustments in flight just by shifting weight make you a little more elusive than when you're on the ground. While airborne and with your jet pack Active, you gain a dodge bonus of +1 to your Reflex Defense. This bonus stacks with other applicable dodge bonuses, and you lose all dodge bonuses when you would lose a Dexterity bonus to your Reflex Defense.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"25d99948c9cb41ad","tags":["defender","evasion","mobility","pilot","scaling","striker","survivability","sustained_damage","tree_25d99948c9cb41ad","uncategorized_talent","vehicle"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"mechanicsMode":"passive_reference","applicationScope":"jetpack_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"requiresSelectedChoice":false,"phase24TacticalRangedMilitaryCleanup":{"phase":"T24","tree":"Jumptrooper","status":"cleaned_runtime_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Unsafe passive/ActiveEffect data removed. Talent is represented by action cards, attack options, hit/critical riders, or explicit manual metadata as appropriate."},"combatActions":[{"id":"reflexive-tilting","name":"Reflexive Tilting","label":"Reflexive Tilting","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"While airborne with your jet pack active, gain a +1 dodge bonus to Reflex Defense. This is contextual and should not alter always-on Reflex.","notes":"While airborne with your jet pack active, gain a +1 dodge bonus to Reflex Defense. This is contextual and should not alter always-on Reflex.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Airborne","Jet pack active","+1 dodge Reflex"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":""}],"manualResolution":true}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.429Z","detectedPredicates":["defense.reflex"]}}}
{"_id":"d49ca4c47e704a96","name":"Defensive Stance","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"Once per encounter as a Reaction to a melee attack made against you, you gain a Damage Reduction score equal to your Base Attack Bonus against that attack.","benefit":"Once per encounter as a Reaction to a melee attack made against you, you gain a Damage Reduction score equal to your Base Attack Bonus against that attack.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"fc978e442f544dbe","tags":["action_economy","damage_reduction","defender","defense","melee","offense_melee","reaction","steady","striker","tree_fc978e442f544dbe","uncategorized_talent","phase-t27-reviewed"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"defensive-stance","name":"Defensive Stance","label":"Defensive Stance","actionType":"reaction","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reaction","useLabel":"React / Note","description":"Once per encounter as a Reaction to a melee attack, gain DR equal to your Base Attack Bonus against that attack.","notes":"Once per encounter as a Reaction to a melee attack, gain DR equal to your Base Attack Bonus against that attack.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Once per encounter"],"requiredContext":["Reaction timing must be valid"],"targetHint":"","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{"reactionKey":"defensiveStance","trigger":"ON_ATTACK_DECLARED"}}],"rules":[],"mechanicsMode":"contextual","applicationScope":"force_lightsaber_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"manualResolution":true,"phase27JediLightsaberMysticCleanup":{"phase":"T27","tree":"Defensive Duelist","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"notes":"Jedi/lightsaber/Mystic leftover pass removed embedded effects and surfaces activation/timing/target context through action cards or resolver rule