{"_id":"d9cb414fe4734507","name":"Mass Cloning","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"You specialize in creating large groups of clones from a single source at one time. The table below determines the increase to the DC modifier. Note, you must have a number of Cloning Tanks equal to the number of clones you wish to simultaneously create prior to attempting a .","benefit":"You specialize in creating large groups of clones from a single source at one time. The table below determines the increase to the DC modifier. Note, you must have a number of Cloning Tanks equal to the number of clones you wish to simultaneously create prior to attempting a .","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"8e44e56069274319","tags":["biotech","cloning","control","crafting","defender","science","tanking","trap","tree_8e44e56069274319","uncategorized_talent","medical","phase-t29-reviewed"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"mass-cloning","name":"Mass Cloning","label":"Mass Cloning","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"You specialize in creating large groups of clones from a single source at one time. The table below determines the increase to the DC modifier. Note, you must have a number of Cloning Tanks equal to the number of clones you wish to simultaneously create prior to attempting a .","notes":"Mass cloning project reference. Requires enough cloning tanks and applies the table-based DC increase; no actor passive bonus is granted.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Knowledge (Life Sciences)"}],"resources":["Multiple clones","Cloning tanks","DC increase table"],"requiredContext":["Cloning project with multiple simultaneous clones"],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action_reference","applicationScope":"runtime_skill_crafting_medical_computer_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase29TechMedicalMicrotreeCleanup":{"phase":"T29","tree":"Cloner","status":"reviewed_manual_or_runtime_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Tech/medical/science microtree pass removed unsafe passive rows and surfaces crafting, cloning, poison, computer, droid-command, and treatment effects as truthful action/reference cards."}}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.430Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"e09d40421ade49e8","name":"Binding Sickle","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"When you miss with an attack made with a Chain Sickle, or fail a Grapple attempt made with one, the target of that attack or attempt takes damage equal to your Dexterity modifier (minimum +1). Homebrew Reference Book: Dathomir Field Guide","benefit":"When you miss with an attack made with a Chain Sickle, or fail a Grapple attempt made with one, the target of that attack or attempt takes damage equal to your Dexterity modifier (minimum +1). Homebrew Reference Book: Dathomir Field Guide","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"ad16f3e5f4f7441b","tags":["exotic_weapon","ranged_control","spellcasting","striker","tree_ad16f3e5f4f7441b","uncategorized_talent","witchcraft"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"mechanicsMode":"manual_or_runtime","applicationScope":"force_user_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase22ForceCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Dathomiri Witch","status":"cleaned_manual_or_future_runtime","notes":"Removed unsafe migrated static modifiers/effects. Talent requires Force-user activation, target, Force Point, suite, item, or encounter context and must not mutate actor totals passively."}}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.431Z","detectedPredicates":[],"forceTalentCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Dathomiri Witch","status":"cleaned_manual_or_future_runtime"}}}}
{"_id":"e6055a514a784387","name":"Akk Dog Master","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":", Commanding Officer, Inspire Loyalty, or Reconnaissance Team Leader Your Followers gain an additional Feat, which they must meet the prerequisites for, and another Feat every 3rd level (as per a normal character). Additionally, your Followers now benefit from changes to their Ability Scores and bonus Feats from their Species; if your Follower's Species does not change their Ability Scores, you can raise a single one of their Abilities from a 10 to a 12. Prerequisite: , Commanding Officer, Inspire Loyalty, or Reconnaissance Team Leader When commanding your Followers, the type they gain is increased by one step (a Swift Action allows a Move Action, a Move Action allows a Standard Action, and a Standard Action allows a Full-Round Action). Additionally, your Followers gain Hit Points equal to their Constitution modifier times your Heroic Level. Prerequisite: , Commanding Officer, Inspire Loyalty, or Reconnaissance Team Leader A number of times per encounter equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum 1), your Followers gain a Swift Action that can be used as normal. Additionally, your Followers gain a number of Trained Skills equal to their Intelligence score, and may take regular Actions instead of Follower Actions (you still must spend the equivalent Action for your Followers).","benefit":", Commanding Officer, Inspire Loyalty, or Reconnaissance Team Leader Your Followers gain an additional Feat, which they must meet the prerequisites for, and another Feat every 3rd level (as per a normal character). Additionally, your Followers now benefit from changes to their Ability Scores and bonus Feats from their Species; if your Follower's Species does not change their Ability Scores, you can raise a single one of their Abilities from a 10 to a 12. Prerequisite: , Commanding Officer, Inspire Loyalty, or Reconnaissance Team Leader When commanding your Followers, the type they gain is increased by one step (a Swift Action allows a Move Action, a Move Action allows a Standard Action, and a Standard Action allows a Full-Round Action). Additionally, your Followers gain Hit Points equal to their Constitution modifier times your Heroic Level. Prerequisite: , Commanding Officer, Inspire Loyalty, or Reconnaissance Team Leader A number of times per encounter equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum 1), your Followers gain a Swift Action that can be used as normal. Additionally, your Followers gain a number of Trained Skills equal to their Intelligence score, and may take regular Actions instead of Follower Actions (you still must spend the equivalent Action for your Followers).","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"37f3554a2f30425a","tags":["action_economy","beast_companion","controller","leader","mobility","mount","move_action","new_action","standard_action","striker","support","survival","sustained_damage","swift_action","tree_37f3554a2f30425a","uncategorized_talent"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.431Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.when-hit"]}}}
{"_id":"e9541e13afbb4a41","name":"Steady Strike","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"You are always considered to be engaged in melee combat for the purposes of ranged attacks made against you, inflicting a -5 penalty to such attacks without the Precise Shot feat. As a Reaction to a failed melee attack made against you while Fighting Defensively, you can move a single square in any direction. This movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity. A number of times per encounter equal to your Dexterity modifier (minimum 1), you can make a single melee attack as a Free Action when Fighting Defensively. You cannot make an attack in this way more than once per round.","benefit":"You are always considered to be engaged in melee combat for the purposes of ranged attacks made against you, inflicting a -5 penalty to such attacks without the Precise Shot feat. As a Reaction to a failed melee attack made against you while Fighting Defensively, you can move a single square in any direction. This movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity. A number of times per encounter equal to your Dexterity modifier (minimum 1), you can make a single melee attack as a Free Action when Fighting Defensively. You cannot make an attack in this way more than once per round.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"fc978e442f544dbe","tags":["action_economy","controller","defense","melee","mobility","offense_melee","positioning","precision","ranged","reaction","steady","sustained_damage","tree_fc978e442f544dbe","uncategorized_talent","phase-t27-reviewed"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"steady-strike","name":"Steady Strike","label":"Steady Strike","actionType":"free","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"You are always considered to be engaged in melee combat for the purposes of ranged attacks made against you, inflicting a -5 penalty to such attacks without the Precise Shot feat. As a Reaction to a failed melee attack made against you while Fighting Defensively, you can move a single square in any direction. This movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity. A number of times per encounter equal to your Dexterity modifier (minimum 1), you can make a single melee attack as a Free Action when Fighting Defensively. You cannot make an attack in this way more than once per round.","notes":"You are always considered to be engaged in melee combat for the purposes of ranged attacks made against you, inflicting a -5 penalty to such attacks without the Precise Shot feat. As a Reaction to a failed melee attack made against you while Fighting Defensively, you can move a single square in any direction. This movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity. A number of times per encounter equal to your Dexterity modifier (minimum 1), you can make a single melee attack as a Free Action when Fighting Defensively. You cannot make an attack in this way more than once per round.","relatedSkills":[],"resources":["Once per round"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"mechanicsMode":"contextual","applicationScope":"force_lightsaber_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"manualResolution":true,"phase27JediLightsaberMysticCleanup":{"phase":"T27","tree":"Defensive Duelist","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"notes":"Jedi/lightsaber/Mystic leftover pass removed embedded effects and surfaces activation/timing/target context through action cards or resolver rules."}}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.431Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.with-melee","attack.with-ranged","turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"ea6ee6fad799491e","name":"Jedi Healer","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Trained in Knowledge (Life Sciences)","description":"You may reroll any Treat Injury check, but the result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse. In addition, you can use the First Aid, Treat Disease, Treat Poison, and Treat Radiation applications without the requisite Medical Kit or Medpac. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook You are Trained in the Treat Injury skill. Additionally, patients under your care move +1 step along the Condition Track as a result of a successful Treat Injury check or activation of the Vital Transfer Force Power.","benefit":"You may reroll any Treat Injury check, but the result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse. In addition, you can use the First Aid, Treat Disease, Treat Poison, and Treat Radiation applications without the requisite Medical Kit or Medpac. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook You are Trained in the Treat Injury skill. Additionally, patients under your care move +1 step along the Condition Track as a result of a successful Treat Injury check or activation of the Vital Transfer Force Power.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"e99cfa9db8493573","tags":["condition_removal","controller","feat_chain","force","force_capacity","force_control","force_power_synergy","force_support","healing","investigation","jedi_healer","knowledge","light_side","medicine","mobility","poison","skills","striker","support","talent_chain","tree_e99cfa9db8493573","uncategorized_talent","phase-t27-reviewed"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"jedi-healer","name":"Jedi Healer","label":"Jedi Healer","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"You may reroll any Treat Injury check, but the result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse. In addition, you can use the First Aid, Treat Disease, Treat Poison, and Treat Radiation applications without the requisite Medical Kit or Medpac. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook You are Trained in the Treat Injury skill. Additionally, patients under your care move +1 step along the Condition Track as a result of a successful Treat Injury check or activation of the Vital Transfer Force Power.","notes":"You may reroll any Treat Injury check, but the result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse. In addition, you can use the First Aid, Treat Disease, Treat Poison, and Treat Radiation applications without the requisite Medical Kit or Medpac. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook You are Trained in the Treat Injury skill. Additionally, patients under your care move +1 step along the Condition Track as a result of a successful Treat Injury check or activation of the Vital Transfer Force Power.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Treat Injury"}],"resources":[],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"mechanicsMode":"contextual","applicationScope":"force_lightsaber_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","requiresRuntimeContext":true,"manualResolution":true,"phase27JediLightsaberMysticCleanup":{"phase":"T27","tree":"Jedi Consular","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"notes":"Jedi/lightsaber/Mystic leftover pass removed embedded effects and surfaces activation/timing/target context through action cards or resolver rules."}}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.431Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"ebc1d6e79fa543c9","name":"Steady Hands","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Trained in Treat Injury","description":"After successfully performing the Revivify application of the Treat Injury skill, the target of your Revivify gains a number of Bonus Hit Points equal to 5 + your Character Level. These Bonus Hit Points last until the end of the encounter (at which point any remaining Bonus Hit Points are lost), and any damage dealt to that target comes out of Bonus Hit Points first. When using the Aid Another Action to aid a character with their Treat Injury check, you grant an additional +2 bonus for every 5 points by which you exceed the DC to assist. You can attempt the First Aid application of the Treat Injury skill without the use of a Medpac. However, doing so imposes a -5 penalty to the check. Choose a single method of medical treatment (Treat Disease, Treat Poison, or Treat Radiation). You may choose to reroll any Treat Injury check to perform that application, keeping the better of the two results. You may select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select this Talent, it applies to a different method of medical treatment. Prerequisite: When performing the First Aid or Heal Damage applications of the Treat Injury skill, you may choose to reroll any Treat Injury check to perform that application, but the result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse. Once per encounter as a Free Action, you reduce the Treat Injury DC for all applications of the skill by your Intelligence modifier (minimum 1) until the start of your next turn. Additionally, when performing the Critical Care application of the Treat Injury skill, you take a -3 penalty to subsequent attempts at Critical Care in the last 24 hours, instead of the normal -5 penalty.","benefit":"After successfully performing the Revivify application of the Treat Injury skill, the target of your Revivify gains a number of Bonus Hit Points equal to 5 + your Character Level. These Bonus Hit Points last until the end of the encounter (at which point any remaining Bonus Hit Points are lost), and any damage dealt to that target comes out of Bonus Hit Points first. When using the Aid Another Action to aid a character with their Treat Injury check, you grant an additional +2 bonus for every 5 points by which you exceed the DC to assist. You can attempt the First Aid application of the Treat Injury skill without the use of a Medpac. However, doing so imposes a -5 penalty to the check. Choose a single method of medical treatment (Treat Disease, Treat Poison, or Treat Radiation). You may choose to reroll any Treat Injury check to perform that application, keeping the better of the two results. You may select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select this Talent, it applies to a different method of medical treatment. Prerequisite: When performing the First Aid or Heal Damage applications of the Treat Injury skill, you may choose to reroll any Treat Injury check to perform that application, but the result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse. Once per encounter as a Free Action, you reduce the Treat Injury DC for all applications of the skill by your Intelligence modifier (minimum 1) until the start of your next turn. Additionally, when performing the Critical Care application of the Treat Injury skill, you take a -3 penalty to subsequent attempts at Critical Care in the last 24 hours, instead of the normal -5 penalty.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"c1cf52502cf74435","tags":["action_economy","critical_hit","damage_reduction","feat_chain","healing","leader","medicine","poison","precision","repair","scaling","skills","stability","striker","support","talent_chain","tree_c1cf52502cf74435","uncategorized_talent","medical","treat-injury","phase-t29-reviewed"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"steady-hands","name":"Steady Hands","label":"Steady Hands","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"After successfully performing the Revivify application of the Treat Injury skill, the target of your Revivify gains a number of Bonus Hit Points equal to 5 + your Character Level. These Bonus Hit Points last until the end of the encounter (at which point any remaining Bonus Hit Points are lost), and any damage dealt to that target comes out of Bonus Hit Points first. When using the Aid Another Action to aid a character with their Treat Injury check, you grant an additional +2 bonus for every 5 points by which you exceed the DC to assist. You can attempt the First Aid application of the Treat Injury skill without the use of a Medpac. However, doing so imposes a -5 penalty to the check. Choose a single method of medical treatment (Treat Disease, Treat Poison, or Treat Radiation). You may choose to reroll any Treat Injury check to perform that application, keeping the better of the two results. You may select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select this Talent, it applies to a different method of medical treatment. Prerequisite: When performing the First Aid or Heal Damage applications of the Treat Injury skill, you may choose to reroll any Treat Injury check to perform that application, but the result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse. Once per encounter as a Free Action, you reduce the Treat Injury DC for all applications of the skill by your Intelligence modifier (minimum 1) until the start of your next turn. Additionally, when performing the Critical Care application of the Treat Injury skill, you take a -3 penalty to subsequent attempts at Critical Care in the last 24 hours, instead of the normal -5 penalty.","notes":"Treatment-tree reference. The current compendium text is merged from multiple medical talents; resolve the specific Treat Injury application/reroll/aid/critical-care benefit being used at the table rather than applying a passive defense bonus.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Treat Injury"}],"resources":["Treat Injury application","Revivify / First Aid / Heal Damage / Critical Care context"],"requiredContext":["Using the relevant Treat Injury application"],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action_reference","applicationScope":"runtime_skill_crafting_medical_computer_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase29TechMedicalMicrotreeCleanup":{"phase":"T29","tree":"Treatment","status":"reviewed_manual_or_runtime_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Tech/medical/science microtree pass removed unsafe passive rows and surfaces crafting, cloning, poison, computer, droid-command, and treatment effects as truthful action/reference cards."}}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.432Z","detectedPredicates":["attack.when-hit","turn.once-per-round"]}}}
{"_id":"f2df5596a9db40c1","name":"Blackguard Initiate","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"You have learned to utilize the abilities of the Force Traditions you study. Select one Force Power; you may spend a Swift Action to replace a power in your Force Power Suite (that has not been expended) with the chosen Force Power. If you do not spend this Force Power before the end of the encounter, it is lost and the replaced power returns to your Force Power Suite. You may activate this Talent a number of times per encounter equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum 1). This Talent may be selected multiple times. Each time you select this Talent, you must choose a different Force Power. Prerequisite: You are a stalwart defender of The Blackguard. As a Standard Action, you can grant yourself a bonus to your Defenses equal to your Dark Side Score or Wisdom modifier (whichever is lower). However, while this effect is active, you suffer a penalty to your attack rolls equal to your Dark Side Score. This effect lasts a number of rounds equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum 1 round). Prerequisite: , Sneak Attack","benefit":"You have learned to utilize the abilities of the Force Traditions you study. Select one Force Power; you may spend a Swift Action to replace a power in your Force Power Suite (that has not been expended) with the chosen Force Power. If you do not spend this Force Power before the end of the encounter, it is lost and the replaced power returns to your Force Power Suite. You may activate this Talent a number of times per encounter equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum 1). This Talent may be selected multiple times. Each time you select this Talent, you must choose a different Force Power. Prerequisite: You are a stalwart defender of The Blackguard. As a Standard Action, you can grant yourself a bonus to your Defenses equal to your Dark Side Score or Wisdom modifier (whichever is lower). However, while this effect is active, you suffer a penalty to your attack rolls equal to your Dark Side Score. This effect lasts a number of rounds equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum 1 round). Prerequisite: , Sneak Attack","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"d2535361d1b146cd","tags":["action_economy","bodyguard","dark_side","defender","defense","force","force_capacity","force_defense","force_offense","force_power_synergy","leader","mobility","new_action","precision","scaling","standard_action","sustained_damage","swift_action","tree_d2535361d1b146cd","uncategorized_talent","phase-t28-reviewed"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"mechanicsMode":"manual_or_runtime","applicationScope":"combat_action_or_force_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"blackguard-initiate","name":"Blackguard Initiate","label":"Blackguard Initiate","actionType":"standard","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"You have learned to utilize the abilities of the Force Traditions you study. Select one Force Power; you may spend a Swift Action to replace a power in your Force Power Suite (that has not been expended) with the chosen Force Power. If you do not spend this Force Power before the end of the encounter, it is lost and the replaced power returns to your Force Power Suite. You may activate this Talent a number of times per encounter equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum 1). This Talent may be selected multiple times. Each time you select this Talent, you must choose a different Force Power. Prerequisite: You are a stalwart defender of The Blackguard. As a Standard Action, you can grant yourself a bonus to your Defenses equal to your Dark Side Score or Wisdom modifier (whichever is lower). However, while this effect is active, you suffer a penalty to your attack rolls equal to your Dark Side Score. This effect lasts a number of rounds equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum 1 round). Prerequisite: , Sneak Attack","notes":"You have learned to utilize the abilities of the Force Traditions you study. Select one Force Power; you may spend a Swift Action to replace a power in your Force Power Suite (that has not been expended) with the chosen Force Power. If you do not spend this Force Power before the end of the encounter, it is lost and the replaced power returns to your Force Power Suite. You may activate this Talent a number of times per encounter equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum 1). This Talent may be selected multiple times. Each time you select this Talent, you must choose a different Force Power. Prerequisite: You are a stalwart defender of The Blackguard. As a Standard Action, you can grant yourself a bonus to your Defenses equal to your Dark Side Score or Wisdom modifier (whichever is lower). However, while this effect is active, you suffer a penalty to your attack rolls equal to your Dark Side Score. This effect lasts a number of rounds equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum 1 round). Prerequisite: , Sneak Attack","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Attack Roll"}],"resources":["Force Power Suite context"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":"","spendAction":true,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"notes":"T28 removed unsafe migrated modifier/effect data. This talent depends on Force-suite, target, equipment, ally, encounter, or table-position context and is surfaced as a truthful manual/runtime card rather than a passive actor mutation.","phase28ForceMicrotraditionCleanup":{"phase":"T28","tree":"Blackguard Wilder","status":"reviewed_contextual_or_manual_card","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Force/special-tradition microtree cleanup. Unsafe always-on rows were removed; final bonuses/effects require player/GM or future dedicated runtime owner."}}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.433Z","detectedPredicates":[]}}}
{"_id":"f785208aa6774cd7","name":"Dark Side Maelstrom","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"You create a wound in The Force itself, tearing open space in a vortex of intense Dark Side energy. Use of this Talent expends the Force Storm and Hatred Force Powers from your Force Power Suite. As a Full-Round Action, you may make a DC 25 Use the Force check. If the check succeeds, you create a within your line of sight one square in size that deals 2d8 Force damage to all targets within its affected area. The maelstrom can only be controlled by the creator and is capable of movement up to 6 squares per round. The maelstrom requires a Use the Force check with a Standard Action to maintain from round to round. The DC to maintain the maelstrom increases by one, the damage increases by +1d8 and it expands in size by one square area each round (1-square becomes 2x2 squares, etc.). If at any time a Use the Force check fails, the maelstrom disperses immediately. If the check fails by 10 or more, the maelstrom turns on its creator, dealing damage equal to its current damage die that round. If you take damage while maintaining , you must succeed on a Use the Force check (DC = current round DC + damage taken) to continue maintaining the Talent and prevent it from turning on its creator. Homebrew Reference Book: Dathomir Field Guide","benefit":"You create a wound in The Force itself, tearing open space in a vortex of intense Dark Side energy. Use of this Talent expends the Force Storm and Hatred Force Powers from your Force Power Suite. As a Full-Round Action, you may make a DC 25 Use the Force check. If the check succeeds, you create a within your line of sight one square in size that deals 2d8 Force damage to all targets within its affected area. The maelstrom can only be controlled by the creator and is capable of movement up to 6 squares per round. The maelstrom requires a Use the Force check with a Standard Action to maintain from round to round. The DC to maintain the maelstrom increases by one, the damage increases by +1d8 and it expands in size by one square area each round (1-square becomes 2x2 squares, etc.). If at any time a Use the Force check fails, the maelstrom disperses immediately. If the check fails by 10 or more, the maelstrom turns on its creator, dealing damage equal to its current damage die that round. If you take damage while maintaining , you must succeed on a Use the Force check (DC = current round DC + damage taken) to continue maintaining the Talent and prevent it from turning on its creator. Homebrew Reference Book: Dathomir Field Guide","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"de95d37c72b1c4cd","tags":["action_economy","battlefield_control","controller","dark_side","dark_side_mastery","force","force_capacity","force_control","force_execution","force_multiplier","force_offense","force_power_synergy","forecast_value","mobility","new_action","positioning","standard_action","striker","sustained_damage","tree_de95d37c72b1c4cd","uncategorized_talent","use_the_force"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"dark-side-maelstrom","name":"Dark Side Maelstrom","label":"Dark Side Maelstrom","actionType":"full-round","cost":1,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"manual","useLabel":"Use / Note","description":"You create a wound in The Force itself, tearing open space in a vortex of intense Dark Side energy. Use of this Talent expends the Force Storm and Hatred Force Powers from your Force Power Suite. As a Full-Round Action, you may make a DC 25 Use the Force check. If the check succeeds, you create a within your line of sight one square in size that deals 2d8 Force damage to all targets within its affected area. The maelstrom can only be controlled by the creator and is capable of movement up to 6 squares per round. The maelstrom requires a Use the Force check with a Standard Action to maintain from round to round. The DC to maintain the maelstrom increases by one, the damage increases by +1d8 and it expands in size by one square area each round (1-square becomes 2x2 squares, etc.). If at any time a Use the Force check fails, the maelstrom disperses immediately. If the check fails by 10 or more, the maelstrom turns on its creator, dealing damage equal to its current damage die that round. If you take damage while maintaining , you must succeed on a Use the Force check (DC = current round DC + damage taken) to continue maintaining the Talent and prevent it from turning on its creator. Homebrew Reference Book: Dathomir Field Guide","notes":"You create a wound in The Force itself, tearing open space in a vortex of intense Dark Side energy. Use of this Talent expends the Force Storm and Hatred Force Powers from your Force Power Suite. As a Full-Round Action, you may make a DC 25 Use the Force check. If the check succeeds, you create a within your line of sight one square in size that deals 2d8 Force damage to all targets within its affected area. The maelstrom can only be controlled by the creator and is capable of movement up to 6 squares per round. The maelstrom requires a Use the Force check with a Standard Action to maintain from round to round. The DC to maintain the maelstrom increases by one, the damage increases by +1d8 and it expands in size by one square area each round (1-square becomes 2x2 squares, etc.). If at any time a Use the Force check fails, the maelstrom disperses immediately. If the check fails by 10 or more, the maelstrom turns on its creator, dealing damage equal to its current damage die that round. If you take damage while maintaining , you must succeed on a Use the Force check (DC = current round DC + damage taken) to continue maintaining the Talent and prevent it from turning on its creator. Homebrew Reference Book: Dathomir Field Guide","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Use the Force"}],"resources":["Expend Force Storm and Hatred","DC 25 Use the Force"],"requiredContext":[],"targetHint":""}],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action","applicationScope":"force_user_runtime_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase22ForceCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Dark Side","status":"combat_action_card","notes":"Removed unsafe migrated static modifiers/effects. Talent requires Force-user activation, target, Force Point, suite, item, or encounter context and must not mutate actor totals passively."}}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.433Z","detectedPredicates":[],"forceTalentCleanup":{"phase":"T22","tree":"Dark Side","status":"combat_action_card"}}}}
{"_id":"fbaab00b6eab02a3","name":"Mercenary's Teamwork","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"Combined Fire, Coordinated Attack","benefit":"You gain a +2 bonus to damage rolls for each ally that has damaged your target since the end of your last turn (to a maximum of +10).","description":{"value":"You gain a +2 bonus to damage rolls for each ally that has damaged your target since the end of your last turn (to a maximum of +10)."},"class":"f62ca2e639cab614","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.combined_fire"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"4007fa87192b5884","tags":["feat-chain","scaling","soldier","striker","support","talent-chain"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"MODIFIER","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[]}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.mercenarys_teamwork"}}}
{"_id":"fd87928650da45fd","name":"Poisoncraft","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"prerequisites":"","description":"Trained in Knowledge (Life Sciences), You have created a simple formula allowing you to revitalize your allies. Once per encounter, as a Standard Action, you can allow an adjacent non-Droid creature to Catch a Second Wind. This Second Wind is not counted towards target's normal daily ability to Catch a Second Wind, but if both are used in the same encounter the target moves -1 Persistent step down the Condition Track at the end of the encounter. The penalties imposed by this Persistent Condition persist until the target takes at least 8 hours to recuperate, during which time the target can't engage in any strenuous activity.","benefit":"Trained in Knowledge (Life Sciences), You have created a simple formula allowing you to revitalize your allies. Once per encounter, as a Standard Action, you can allow an adjacent non-Droid creature to Catch a Second Wind. This Second Wind is not counted towards target's normal daily ability to Catch a Second Wind, but if both are used in the same encounter the target moves -1 Persistent step down the Condition Track at the end of the encounter. The penalties imposed by this Persistent Condition persist until the target takes at least 8 hours to recuperate, during which time the target can't engage in any strenuous activity.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"00cb74839a524276","tags":["action_economy","condition_removal","controller","droid","investigation","knowledge","knowledge_creatures","mobility","new_action","poison","positioning","standard_action","survival","sustained_damage","tree_00cb74839a524276","uncategorized_talent","science","medical","phase-t29-reviewed"],"executionModel":"PASSIVE","subType":"STATE","abilityMeta":{"modifiers":[],"combatActions":[{"id":"poisoncraft","name":"Poisoncraft","label":"Poisoncraft","actionType":"passive","cost":0,"manualResolution":true,"resolutionMode":"reference","useLabel":"Reference","description":"Trained in Knowledge (Life Sciences), You have created a simple formula allowing you to revitalize your allies. Once per encounter, as a Standard Action, you can allow an adjacent non-Droid creature to Catch a Second Wind. This Second Wind is not counted towards target's normal daily ability to Catch a Second Wind, but if both are used in the same encounter the target moves -1 Persistent step down the Condition Track at the end of the encounter. The penalties imposed by this Persistent Condition persist until the target takes at least 8 hours to recuperate, during which time the target can't engage in any strenuous activity.","notes":"Poison crafting / formula reference. Use Treat Injury and the poison CL/object construction rules; any second-wind/medical formula text in the merged source should be adjudicated manually.","relatedSkills":[{"skill":"Treat Injury"},{"skill":"Knowledge (Life Sciences)"}],"resources":["Poison crafting","Treat Injury substitution","Poison Challenge Level"],"requiredContext":["Crafting poison or medical formula"],"targetHint":"","spendAction":false,"ruleData":{}}],"rules":[],"mechanicsMode":"combat_action_reference","applicationScope":"runtime_skill_crafting_medical_computer_context","staticSheetPolicy":"exclude","manualResolution":true,"requiresRuntimeContext":true,"phase29TechMedicalMicrotreeCleanup":{"phase":"T29","tree":"Science","status":"reviewed_manual_or_runtime_context","removedLegacyModifierRows":1,"removedEmbeddedActiveEffects":0,"notes":"Tech/medical/science microtree pass removed unsafe passive rows and surfaces crafting, cloning, poison, computer, droid-command, and treatment effects as truthful action/reference cards."}}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"migratedToState":true,"migrationDate":"2026-03-08T18:22:17.436Z","detectedPredicates":["turn.once-per-round"]}}}
